,322 + 65,7900 = 703,222. \n\nYes, that's the same result. So, all methods give 703,222. Therefore, the product of 731 and 962 is 703,222. \n\nI think that's correct. Let me just verify with a calculator to be 100% sure. But since I don't have a calculator here, maybe approximate. 700\u00d71000 is 700,000. 731 is 31 more, 962 is 38 less. So, the difference from 700,000 would be 31\u00d7962 - 38\u00d7700. Wait, that might not be the right way. Alternatively, the product is 700\u00d7962 + 31\u00d7962. Let's compute that.\n\n700\u00d7962: 700\u00d7900=630,000; 700\u00d762=43,400. So, 630,000 + 43,400 = 673,400.\n\n31\u00d7962: 30\u00d7962=28,860; 1\u00d7962=962. So, 28,860 + 962 = 29,822.\n\nThen, 673,400 + 29,822 = 703,222. Yep, same answer. So, definitely, the product is 703,222. I think that's solid.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 731 and 962 is \\boxed{703222}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 731 and 962, we can use the distributive property and break down the numbers into smaller parts:\n\n1. Express 731 as \\(700 + 31\\) and 962 as \\(1000 - 38\\).\n2. Expand the product using the distributive property:\n   \\[\n   (700 + 31) \\times (1000 - 38) = 700 \\times 1000 + 700 \\times (-38) + 31 \\times 1000 + 31 \\times (-38)\n   \\]\n3. Calculate each term separately:\n   - \\(700 \\times 1000 = 700,000\\)\n   - \\(700 \\times (-38) = -26,600\\)\n   - \\(31 \\times 1000 = 31,000\\)\n   - \\(31 \\times (-38) = -1,178\\)\n4. Combine all the terms:\n   \\[\n   700,000 - 26,600 + 31,000 - 1,178\n   \\]\n5. Perform the arithmetic step by step:\n   - \\(700,000 - 26,600 = 673,400\\)\n   - \\(673,400 + 31,000 = 704,400\\)\n   - \\(704,400 - 1,178 = 703,222\\)\n\nVerification using the standard multiplication algorithm confirms the result. Therefore, the product of 731 and 962 is \\(\\boxed{703222}\\).",
