Then add 17: 7,057 +17=7,074. Wait, that's not matching. Wait, no, this is getting confusing. Maybe I need to approach this differently.\n\nWait, perhaps the confusion arises from how I'm adding the numbers. Let me write them vertically aligned properly:\n\n      131\n    x 742\n    ------\n      917   (131 x 7)\n     91,700  (131 x 40, shifted one position)\n     5,240   (131 x 2, shifted two positions)\n    ------\n     97,202  (sum)\n\nSo, 917 is in the thousands place, 91,700 is in the ten thousands place (since it's shifted one position to the left), and 5,240 is in the thousands place (shifted two positions). Wait, no. Wait, when you multiply by 40, which is 4*10, you shift the partial product one position to the left. Similarly, multiplying by 2, which is 2*100, you shift two positions to the left. So:\n\n- 131 x 7 = 917 (no shift)\n- 131 x 40 = 5,240 (shift one position left: so it's 5,240, which is 5,240)\n- 131 x 2 = 262 (shift two positions left: so it's 2,620)\n\nTherefore, adding:\n\n917 (thousands place)\n+5,240 (hundreds place)\n+2,620 (tens place)\n= 917 + 5,240 + 2,620\n\nLet's compute 917 + 5,240 first. 917 + 5,000 = 5,917. Then 5,917 + 240 = 6,157.\n\nThen add 2,620: 6,157 + 2,620. 6,157 + 2,000 = 8,157. Then 8,157 + 620 = 8,777.\n\nWait, that's 8,777. But that contradicts the previous total of 97,202. Clearly, something is wrong here. Wait, no, I think I messed up the alignment. Let me try again.\n\nWait, in vertical multiplication, each partial product is shifted based on the place value of the multiplier. So:\n\n- Multiplying by 7 (units place): 917, no shift.\n- Multiplying by 40 (tens place): 5,240, shifted one position to the left (so it's 5,240, which is 5,240).\n- Multiplying by 2 (hundreds place): 262, shifted two positions to the left (so it's 2,620).\n\nTherefore, when adding:\n\n917 (no shift)\n+5,240 (shifted left once)\n+2,620 (shifted left twice)\n= 917 + 5,240 + 2,620\n\nBut 917 + 5,240 is 6,157. Then 6,157 + 2,620 is 8,777. But th