\n2 \u00d7 828 = 1,656. Write down 1,656.\n\nMultiply 828 by 1 (tens place of 612):\n\n1 \u00d7 828 = 828. Write down 828, shifted one position to the left.\n\nMultiply 828 by 6 (hundreds place of 612):\n\n6 \u00d7 828 = 4,968. Write down 4,968, shifted two positions to the left.\n\nNow, add them up:\n\n1,656\n\n\u00a0828\n\n+4,968\n\n------\n\nLet's add them step by step.\n\nFirst, add 1,656 and 828:\n\n1,656 + 800 = 2,456\n\n2,456 + 28 = 2,484\n\nThen add 2,484 and 4,968:\n\n2,484 + 4,000 = 6,484\n\n6,484 + 968 = 7,452\n\nSo the result is 7,452. But according to the calculator, it's 59,616. Wait, this is impossible. There must be a mistake in my calculations.\n\nWait, no. Wait, 828 \u00d7 612. Let me compute 828 \u00d7 612:\n\nFirst, 800 \u00d7 600 = 480,000\n\n800 \u00d7 12 = 9,600\n\n28 \u00d7 600 = 16,800\n\n28 \u00d7 12 = 336\n\nAdding all together:\n\n480,000 + 9,600 = 489,600\n\n16,800 + 336 = 17,136\n\n489,600 + 17,136 = 506,736.\n\nWait, so according to this, 828 \u00d7 612 = 506,736. But according to the step-by-step multiplication, it's 7,452. That can't be. There's a mistake here. Wait, no. Wait, 828 \u00d7 612. Let me compute 828 \u00d7 612:\n\nWait, 828 \u00d7 600 = 49,680\n\n828 \u00d7 12 = 9,936\n\n49,680 + 9,936 = 59,616. But according to the other method, it's 506,736. So which one is correct?\n\nWait, I think the problem is that I'm using different numbers. Wait, 828 \u00d7 612. Let me compute 828 \u00d7 612:\n\nFirst, 828 \u00d7 600 = 49,680\n\n828 \u00d7 10 = 8,280\n\n828 \u00d7 2 = 1,656\n\nAdding them together: 49,680 + 8,280 = 57,960; 57,960 + 1,656 = 59,616.\n\nBut when I compute 800 \u00d7 612 = 49,680; 28 \u00d7 612 = 17,136; 49,680 + 17,136 = 66,816. Wait, that's different. Wait, no. Wait, 828 is 800 + 28. So 828 \u00d7 612 = (800 + 28) \u00d7 612 = 800\u00d7612 + 28\u00d7612. 800\u00d7612 = 49,680; 28\u00d7612 = 17,136. Then 49,680 + 17,136 = 66,816. But that's not matching the previous result. So now I'm really confused.\n\nWait, this 