hat's good.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use another decomposition. Let's see, 861 is 800 + 60 + 1, which we already did. Alternatively, 861 is 800 + 60 + 1, so same thing.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the calculator method. But since I don't have a calculator, perhaps another way.\n\nAlternatively, multiply 348 x 861:\n\nLet me write 348 as 300 + 40 + 8.\n\nSo, (300 + 40 + 8) x 861 = 300*861 + 40*861 + 8*861.\n\nCompute each term:\n\n300*861: 300*800=240,000; 300*60=18,000; 300*1=300. So total 240,000 + 18,000 = 258,000 + 300 = 258,300.\n\n40*861: 40*800=32,000; 40*60=2,400; 40*1=40. Total 32,000 + 2,400 = 34,400 + 40 = 34,440.\n\n8*861: 8*800=6,400; 8*60=480; 8*1=8. Total 6,400 + 480 = 6,880 + 8 = 6,888.\n\nNow, add all three results: 258,300 + 34,440 + 6,888.\n\nFirst, 258,300 + 34,440. Let's compute:\n\n258,300 + 30,000 = 288,300\n\n288,300 + 4,440 = 292,740\n\nThen, add 6,888: 292,740 + 6,888.\n\n292,740 + 6,000 = 298,740\n\n298,740 + 888 = 299,628. Again, same result. So that's consistent.\n\nTherefore, the product of 348 and 861 is 299,628.\n\nWait, but just to make sure, let me check with another approach. Maybe breaking down 861 into 800 + 60 + 1, but using another multiplication.\n\nAlternatively, use the distributive property in a different way. Let's see:\n\n348 x 861 = 348 x (800 + 60 + 1) = 348*800 + 348*60 + 348*1, which we already did. So same as before.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the fact that 861 is 800 + 60 + 1, but compute 348*800 first. 348*800. 348*8=2,784, so 2,784*100=278,400. Then 348*60=20,880. Then 348*1=348. Then add them all. Which is the same as before.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the standard algorithm step by step.\n\nMultiplying 348 by 861:\n\nFirst, multiply 348 by 1: 348.\n\nThen, multiply 348 by 6 (tens place): 2,088. Shift one position: 20,880.\n\nThen, multiply 348 by 8 (hundreds place): 2,784. Shift two positions: 278,400.\n\nNow, add them up:\n\n348\n\n20,880\n\n278,400\n\nAdding these:\n\nStart with 348 + 20,880 = 21,228.\n\nThen 21,228 + 278,400 = 299,628.\n\nYes, same result. So all methods lead to 299,628. Therefore, I can be confident that the product of 348 and 861 is 299,628.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 348 and 861 is \\boxed{299628}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 348 and 861, we can use the standard multiplication method:\n\n1. Multiply 348 by the rightmost digit (1):\n   \\[\n   348 \\times 1 = 348\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 348 by the middle digit (6), shifting one position to the left:\n   \\[\n   348 \\times 6 = 2088 \\quad \\text{(shifted one position: 20880)}\n   \\]\n3. Multiply 348 by the leftmost digit (8), shifting two positions to the left:\n   \\[\n   348 \\times 8 = 2784 \\quad \\text{(shifted two positions: 278400)}\n   \\]\n\nNext, we add the partial products:\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n  348 \\\\\n 20880 \\\\\n278400 \\\\\n\\hline\n299628 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nBreaking down the addition step-by-step:\n1. Add the first partial product (348) and the second partial product (20880):\n   \\[\n   348 + 20880 = 21228\n   \\]\n2. Add the result to the third partial product (278400):\n   \\[\n   21228 + 278400 = 299628\n   \\]\n\nThus, the product of 348 and 861 is \\(\\boxed{299628}\\).",
