\nLet me write it out again:\n\n        758\n      x 447\n      -------\n\nFirst, multiply 758 by 7:\n\n758\nx   7\n-----\n5306\n\nThen, multiply 758 by 4 (tens place):\n\n   758\nx   4\n-----\n3032\nShifted one position: 30320\n\nThen, multiply 758 by 4 (hundreds place):\n\n   758\nx   4\n-----\n3032\nShifted two positions: 303200\n\nNow, adding 5306 + 30320 + 303200.\n\nLet me add 5306 + 30320 first:\n\n5306 + 30320:\n\n5000 + 30000 = 35000\n\n306 + 320 = 626\n\n35000 + 626 = 35626\n\nThen, add 303200:\n\n35626 + 303200:\n\n35626 + 300000 = 335626\n\n335626 + 3200 = 338826\n\nYes, same result. So, seems like 338,826 is the correct product.\n\nAlternatively, maybe check with another multiplication. Let's take 758 x 447. Let's use the fact that 447 = 450 - 3. So, 758 x 450 - 758 x 3.\n\nCompute 758 x 450 first. 758 x 450. Let's compute 758 x 400 = 303,200 and 758 x 50 = 37,900. So, 303,200 + 37,900 = 341,100.\n\nThen, subtract 758 x 3 = 2,274.\n\nSo, 341,100 - 2,274 = 338,826. Again, same result. That's a good confirmation.\n\nTherefore, I can be confident that the product of 758 and 447 is 338,826.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 758 and 447 is \\boxed{338826}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 758 and 447, we can use the distributive property by breaking down 447 into 400, 40, and 7. Then, multiply 758 by each part and add the results together.\n\n1. Calculate \\( 758 \\times 400 \\):\n   \\[\n   758 \\times 400 = 758 \\times 4 \\times 100 = 3032 \\times 100 = 303200\n   \\]\n\n2. Calculate \\( 758 \\times 40 \\):\n   \\[\n   758 \\times 40 = 758 \\times 4 \\times 10 = 3032 \\times 10 = 30320\n   \\]\n\n3. Calculate \\( 758 \\times 7 \\):\n   \\[\n   758 \\times 7 = 5306\n   \\]\n\n4. Add all the partial products together:\n   \\[\n   303200 + 30320 + 5306\n   \\]\n\n5. First, add \\( 303200 \\) and \\( 30320 \\):\n   \\[\n   303200 + 30320 = 333520\n   \\]\n\n6. Then, add the result to \\( 5306 \\):\n   \\[\n   333520 + 5306 = 338826\n   \\]\n\nThus, the product of 758 and 447 is \\(\\boxed{338826}\\).",
