rms that the product is 157,025.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using a calculator to verify. Since I don't have a calculator here, but let me check with another manual multiplication.\n\nLet me try multiplying 571 by 275 using the standard algorithm step by step.\n\nFirst, write 571 x 275.\n\nMultiply 571 by 5: 2,855.\n\nMultiply 571 by 70: 39,970.\n\nMultiply 571 by 200: 114,200.\n\nAdd them up:\n\n2,855\n\n+39,970\n\n=42,825\n\n42,825 + 114,200 = 157,025.\n\nYes, same result. So, all methods lead to 157,025. Therefore, I can be confident that the product of 571 and 275 is 157,025.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 571 and 275 is \\boxed{157025}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 571 and 275, we can use the standard multiplication method by breaking down the multiplication into parts:\n\n1. Multiply 571 by 5 (the units digit of 275):\n   \\[\n   571 \\times 5 = 2855\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 571 by 70 (the tens digit of 275, which is 7 multiplied by 10):\n   \\[\n   571 \\times 70 = 39970\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 571 by 200 (the hundreds digit of 275, which is 2 multiplied by 100):\n   \\[\n   571 \\times 200 = 114200\n   \\]\n\n4. Add the results of the three multiplications together:\n   \\[\n   2855 + 39970 + 114200\n   \\]\n\n   First, add 2855 and 39970:\n   \\[\n   2855 + 39970 = 42825\n   \\]\n\n   Then, add the result to 114200:\n   \\[\n   42825 + 114200 = 157025\n   \\]\n\nThus, the product of 571 and 275 is \\(\\boxed{157025}\\).",
