her method, such as the difference of squares or other identities, but since these numbers aren't particularly close to each other or to a common base, that might not be helpful. Alternatively, break them into prime factors and multiply, but that might be more time-consuming.\n\nAlternatively, use estimation to check if 764,048 is reasonable. Let's see, 900 x 800 = 720,000. 900 x 48 = 43,200. 1 x 800 = 800. 1 x 48 = 48. So total would be 720,000 + 43,200 + 800 + 48 = 720,000 + 43,200 = 763,200; 763,200 + 800 = 764,000; 764,000 + 48 = 764,048. Yep, that's the same.\n\nSo all methods lead to the same answer. Therefore, I can be confident that the product of 901 and 848 is 764,048.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 901 and 848 is \\boxed{764048}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 901 and 848, we can use the distributive property:\n\nFirst, break down 848 into 800, 40, and 8. Then multiply 901 by each part and sum the results:\n\n1. Calculate \\( 901 \\times 800 \\):\n   \\[\n   901 \\times 800 = 901 \\times 8 \\times 100 = 7208 \\times 100 = 720800\n   \\]\n\n2. Calculate \\( 901 \\times 40 \\):\n   \\[\n   901 \\times 40 = 901 \\times 4 \\times 10 = 3604 \\times 10 = 36040\n   \\]\n\n3. Calculate \\( 901 \\times 8 \\):\n   \\[\n   901 \\times 8 = 7208\n   \\]\n\n4. Sum the results:\n   \\[\n   720800 + 36040 + 7208\n   \\]\n\n5. Add step-by-step:\n   \\[\n   720800 + 36040 = 756840\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   756840 + 7208 = 764048\n   \\]\n\nThus, the product of 901 and 848 is \\(\\boxed{764048}\\).",
