is 467,016.\n\nTherefore, the total product is 467,016.\n\nBut wait, earlier when I did the partial products:\n\nFirst partial product:7,656\n\nSecond:76,560\n\nThird:382,800\n\nAdding them:7,656 +76,560=84,216; 84,216 +382,800=467,016. Yes, that's correct.\n\nSo the correct product is 467,016.\n\nBut earlier, when I thought I had 159,842, that was a mistake because I incorrectly calculated 4 x957 as 3,800 instead of 3,828. So that was the error.\n\nTherefore, the correct product of 957 and 488 is 467,016.\n\nLet me verify this with another method to be sure. Let's use the standard multiplication algorithm correctly.\n\nMultiplying 957 by 488:\n\nFirst, write 957 x 488.\n\nStart with the ones digit:8\n\n957 x8=7,656\n\nNext, the tens digit:8, so multiply 957 by8 and add a zero:7,6560\n\nThen, the hundreds digit:4, multiply 957 by4 and add two zeros:38,2800\n\nNow, add them up:\n\n7,656\n\n76,560\n\n382,800\n\nAdding step by step:\n\nFirst, 7,656 +76,560=84,216\n\nThen, 84,216 +382,800=467,016\n\nYes, that's correct.\n\nAlternatively, using the distributive property:\n\n957 x488=957x(500-12)=957x500 -957x12=478,500 -11,484=467,016.\n\nYes, that matches.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is 467,016.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 957 and 488 is \\boxed{467016}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 957 and 488, we can use the distributive property:\n\n1. Break down 488 into 500 - 12.\n2. Calculate each part separately:\n   - \\( 957 \\times 500 = 478500 \\)\n   - \\( 957 \\times 12 = 11484 \\)\n3. Subtract the results:\n   - \\( 478500 - 11484 = 467016 \\)\n\nWe can also verify this using the standard multiplication method:\n1. Multiply 957 by each digit of 488 (8, 80, 400) and adjust the place values:\n   - \\( 957 \\times 8 = 7656 \\)\n   - \\( 957 \\times 80 = 76560 \\)\n   - \\( 957 \\times 400 = 382800 \\)\n2. Add the partial products:\n   - \\( 7656 + 76560 = 84216 \\)\n   - \\( 84216 + 382800 = 467016 \\)\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 957 and 48