So that works. \n\nAlternatively, maybe using another decomposition. Let's see, 499 is 500 -1, so 332 \u00d7 499 = 332 \u00d7 (500 -1) = 332\u00d7500 - 332. Which is exactly what I did first. So that's the same as the first method. \n\nAlternatively, maybe using the formula (a - b)(a + b) = a\u00b2 - b\u00b2, but I don't think that applies here. Wait, 499 is 500 -1, so maybe not. Alternatively, 499 is 500 -1, so that's already factored. So the first method is the way to go. \n\nAlternatively, maybe using the standard multiplication algorithm step by step. Let me try that again. \n\nMultiplying 332 by 499. \n\nStart with the units digit: 9. Multiply 332 by 9. \n\n332 \u00d7 9: 2\u00d79=18, carryover 1. 3\u00d79=27 +1=28, carryover 2. 3\u00d79=27 +2=29. So that's 2988. Write down 2988.\n\nNext, the tens digit is 9. Multiply 332 by 9, but since it's the tens place, we need to shift one position to the left. So 2988 becomes 29880. \n\nThen, the hundreds digit is 4. Multiply 332 by 4. 2\u00d74=8, 3\u00d74=12 +0=12, 3\u00d74=12 +0=12. So 1212. Then multiply by 100 to shift two positions: 121200.\n\nNow add them all together: 2988 + 29880 + 121200.\n\nFirst, 2988 + 29880. Let's compute 2988 + 29880. 29880 + 2000 = 31880. 31880 + 988 = 32868.\n\nThen add 121200 to 32868. 32868 + 121200. 32868 + 100000 = 132868. 132868 + 21200 = 154,068. Wait, that doesn't match the previous total. Wait, hold on, maybe I messed up here. Wait, 32,868 + 121,200. Let's do 32,868 + 100,000 = 132,868. Then add 21,200: 132,868 + 21,200 = 154,068. Wait, but earlier when I added 29,880 + 132,800, I got 162,680. Wait, no, that's not right. Wait, no, in the first method, when I added 29,880 + 132,800, that was 162,680. But here, adding 29,868 + 121,200, which is 154,068. Wait, that's conflicting. Wait, no, hold on. Wait, in the first step, when I did the multiplication, I think I might have made a mistake. Let me check again.\n\nWait, in the standard multiplication method, when I multiplied 332 by 9 (