170 + 800 = 970. So 26000 + 970 = 26,970. Then add 186,000. 26,970 + 186,000. 20,000 + 186,000 = 206,000. 6,970 + 6,000 = 12,970. So 206,000 + 12,970 = 218,970. But this contradicts the previous results. So where is the mistake?\n\nWait, maybe the alignment is wrong. Let's write it out properly:\n\n        310\n      x 687\n      ------\n        2170  (310 x 7)\n       24800  (310 x 8, shifted one)\n      186000  (310 x 6, shifted two)\n      ------\n      218,970\n\nWait, but according to the first method, it should be 212,970. So there's a conflict here. Which one is correct?\n\nWait, let's check with another method. Let's compute 310 x 687. Let's use the fact that 310 x 687 = 310 x (700 - 13) = 310*700 - 310*13. \n\n310*700: 310*7=2170, so 2170*100=217,000.\n\n310*13: 310*10=3,100; 310*3=930. So 3,100 + 930=4,030.\n\nSubtracting: 217,000 - 4,030 = 212,970. So that's 212,970. \n\nBut when I did the standard multiplication, I got 218,970. So there's a discrepancy. Therefore, my standard multiplication must have an error. Let me check again.\n\nWait, perhaps I made a mistake in the standard multiplication. Let's do it step by step:\n\nFirst, multiply 310 by 7:\n\n310\n\nx  7\n\n------\n\n2170\n\nThat's correct.\n\nThen multiply 310 by 8:\n\n310\n\nx  8\n\n------\n\n2480\n\nBut since it's the tens place, we need to shift one position to the left, so it becomes 24800.\n\nThen multiply 310 by 6:\n\n310\n\nx  6\n\n------\n\n1860\n\nShift two positions to the left, so 186000.\n\nNow, adding:\n\n2170\n\n24800\n\n186000\n\nLet's add them:\n\nFirst, 2170 + 24800. Let's compute 2170 + 24800. 2000 + 24000 = 26000. 170 + 800 = 970. So 26000 + 970 = 26,970.\n\nThen add 186,000. 26,970 + 186,000. 20,000 + 186,000 = 206,000. 6,970 + 6,000 = 12,970. So 206,000 + 12,970 = 218,970.\n\nBut according to the other methods, it's 212,970. So where is the mistake?\n\nWait, maybe the alignment when adding is wrong. Let me write all three numbers with proper alignment:\n\n    2170\n\n  +24800\n\n+186000\n\nLet's add them:\n\nStart with 2170 + 24800. 2170 + 24800 = 26,970.\n\nThen add 186,000. 26,970 + 186,000. Let's do 26,970 + 186,000. 26,970 + 180,000 = 206,970. Then add 6,000: 206,970 + 6,000 = 212,970. Wait, that's different. Wait, no. Wait, 26,970 + 186,000. Let's break it down:\n\n26,970 + 186,000 = (20,000 + 6,970) + (180,000 + 6,000) = (20,000 + 180,000) + (6,970 + 6,000) = 200,000 + 12,970 = 212,970. Ah! There we go. So I must have added incorrectly earlier. So 26,970 + 186,000 = 212,970. Then adding the 2170? Wait, no. Wait, the first two numbers (2170 and 24800) sum to 26,970. Then adding 186,000 gives 212,970. So that's correct. So my mistake earlier was adding 26,970 + 186,000 as 218,970, but actually, 26,970 + 186,000 is 212,970. Because 26,970 + 186,000 = 212,970. So that aligns with the first method. \n\nSo the correct total is 212,970. Therefore, the standard multiplication method, when done correctly, also gives 212,970. So my earlier mistake was in the addition step where I incorrectly summed 26,970 + 186,000 as 218,970 instead of 212,970. That was the error.\n\nTherefore, all three methods confirm that the product of 310 and 687 is 212,970. \n\nJust to be thorough, let me compute it using another approach. Let's use the original numbers and see if there's another way. For example, 310 x 687. Let's compute 310 x 700 = 217,000. Then subtract 310 x 13 = 4,030. So 217,000 - 4,030 = 212,970. Yep, same result.\n\nAlternatively, using the distributive property again: 310 x 687 = 300 x 687 + 10 x 687. 300 x 687: 3 x 687 = 2061, times 100 is 206,100. 10 x 687 = 6,870. Adding them gives 206,100 + 6,870 = 212,970. \n\nSo all methods lead to the same answer. Therefore, I can be confident that the product of 310 and 687 is 212,970.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 310 and 687 is \\boxed{212970}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 310 and 687, we can use the distributive property:\n\n1. Break down 310 into 300 and 10:\n   \\[\n   310 \\times 687 = (300 + 10) \\times 687\n   \\]\n2. Distribute the multiplication:\n   \\[\n   300 \\times 687 + 10 \\times 687\n   \\]\n3. Calculate each part separately:\n   - For \\(300 \\times 687\\):\n     \\[\n     3 \\times 687 = 2061 \\quad \\text{(since } 3 \\times 600 = 1800\\text{ and } 3 \\times 87 = 261\\text{)}\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     2061 \\times 100 = 206100\n     \\]\n   - For \\(10 \\times 687\\):\n     \\[\n     10 \\times 687 = 6870\n     \\]\n4. Add the results together:\n   \\[\n   206100 + 6870 = 212970\n   \\]\n\nVerification using the standard multiplication method:\n- Multiply 310 by 7, 8, and 6 separately and then shift appropriately:\n  \\[\n  \\begin{array}{r}\n    310 \\\\\n  \\times 687 \\\\\n  \\hline\n    2170 \\quad \\text{(310 x 7)} \\\\\n   24800 \\quad \\text{(310 x 8, shifted one position)} \\\\\n  186000 \\quad \\text{(310 x 6, shifted two positions)} \\\\\n  \\hline\n  212970 \\quad \\text{(sum of the partial products)}\n  \\end{array}\n  \\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 310 and 687 is \\(\\boxed{212970}\\).",
