21 and multiplying step by step. But I think the methods above have confirmed that 429,825 is the correct answer. \n\nTherefore, the product of 825 and 521 is 429,825.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 825 and 521 is \\boxed{429825}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 825 and 521, we can use the distributive property:\n\nFirst, break down each number into smaller parts:\n- \\(825 = 800 + 25\\)\n- \\(521 = 500 + 21\\)\n\nNow, apply the distributive property:\n\\[\n825 \\times 521 = (800 + 25)(500 + 21)\n\\]\n\nCalculate each part separately:\n1. \\(800 \\times 500 = 400,000\\)\n2. \\(800 \\times 21 = 16,800\\)\n3. \\(25 \\times 500 = 12,500\\)\n4. \\(25 \\times 21 = 525\\)\n\nAdd all the results together:\n\\[\n400,000 + 16,800 + 12,500 + 525\n\\]\n\nPerform the addition step by step:\n1. \\(400,000 + 16,800 = 416,800\\)\n2. \\(416,800 + 12,500 = 429,300\\)\n3. \\(429,300 + 525 = 429,825\\)\n\nThus, the product of 825 and 521 is \\(\\boxed{429825}\\).",
