he tens place, so it's added as 525. Wait, but 5,250 is 5 thousands, 2 hundreds, 5 tens. So, when shifted one position, it's 5 hundreds, 2 tens, 5 units. So, 525. So, adding 700 (from units place) + 525 (from tens place) + 1575 (from hundreds place). But 700 + 525 is 1,225, and 1,225 + 1,575 is 2,800. But that's not matching the actual product. So, where is the mistake?\n\nWait, maybe the problem is that in the vertical multiplication, the numbers being added are not the partial products as separate numbers, but when you shift them, they are added to the total. Wait, no, in the vertical multiplication, each partial product is a separate number that's being added. Wait, perhaps I need to write it out properly.\n\nLet me try again:\n\nMultiplying 175 by 934:\n\nFirst, multiply 175 by 4 (units digit):\n\n175\n\nx  4\n\n----\n\n700\n\nSo, 700.\n\nThen, multiply 175 by 3 (tens digit), but since it's the tens digit, we add a zero:\n\n175\n\nx  30\n\n----\n\n5250\n\nBut in the vertical multiplication, this is written as 525 shifted one position, so:\n\n      525\n\nThen, multiply 175 by 9 (hundreds digit), add two zeros:\n\n175\n\nx  900\n\n----\n\n15750\n\nShifted two positions, so:\n\n      1575\n\nNow, adding the three partial products:\n\n700\n\n+ 525\n\n+1575\n\nLet's add 700 + 525 first. 700 + 500 = 1,200; 1,200 + 25 = 1,225.\n\nThen, 1,225 + 1,575. 1,225 + 1,500 = 2,725; 2,725 + 75 = 2,800.\n\nBut 2,800 is way too low. But we know the correct answer is 163,450. So, clearly, there's a disconnect here. Wait, maybe I'm misunderstanding the vertical multiplication layout.\n\nWait, perhaps the confusion is because when you do 175 x 934, the partial products are:\n\n- 175 x 4 = 700 (units place)\n\n- 175 x 30 = 5,250 (tens place, so shifted one)\n\n- 175 x 900 = 15,750 (hundreds place, shifted two)\n\nBut when written in the vertical multiplication, the numbers are:\n\n      175\n\n    x 934\n\n    ------\n      6,250  (175 x 4)\n     11,000   (175 x 30)\n    15,875    (175 x 900)\n    ------\n      163,450\n\nBut in this layout, the numbers being added are 6,250; 11,000; and 15,875. Wait, but 6,250 is 175 x 4, which is correct. 11,000 is 175 x 30, which is correct. 15,875 is 175 x 900, which is correct. So, adding those three numbers: 6,250 + 11,000 + 15,875.\n\n6,250 + 11,000 = 17,250. Then, 17,250 + 15,875 = 33,125. Wait, that's 33,125. But that's not 163,450. So, this is conflicting. What's going on here?\n\nWait, no, hold on. Wait, 175 x 4 is 700. But in the vertical multiplication, the first partial product is 6,250. Wait, that's not right. Wait, 175 x 4 is 700, but in the vertical layout, the first partial product is 6,250. That's a mistake. Wait, why is that?\n\nWait, no, actually, in the vertical multiplication, when you multiply by the units digit, you get 700. But in the standard multiplication algorithm, you write the units digit result on the right. So, 175 x 4 = 700. So, you write 0 (units place) and carry over 7. Then, the tens place: 175 x 3 = 525, plus the carried over 7 is 532. Then, hundreds place: 175 x 9 = 1,575. So, the partial products are 700, 532, and 1,575. Then, adding them up: 700 + 532 = 1,232; 1,232 + 1,575 = 2,807. Wait, that's 2,807. But that's not matching either.\n\nWait, now I'm really confused. There must be a mistake in my understanding. Let me check with another method.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use the distributive property again but check each step.\n\nOriginal problem: 175 x 934.\n\nBreaking 175 into 100 + 75.\n\nSo, 100 x 934 = 93,400.\n\n75 x 934. Let's compute that.\n\n75 is 70 + 5.\n\n70 x 934 = 65,380.\n\n5 x 934 = 4,670.\n\nAdding those together: 65,380 + 4,670 = 70,050.\n\nThen, adding to the previous result: 93,400 + 70,050 = 163,450.\n\nOkay, so that gives the same result as before. So, that seems correct.\n\nBut when I tried the vertical multiplication, I was getting confused. Let me try again with the vertical multiplication.\n\nMultiplying 175 by 934:\n\nFirst, write 175 x 934.\n\nStart with the units digit: 4.\n\n175 x 4 = 700. Write down 0, carry over 7.\n\nNext, the tens digit: 3.\n\n175 x 3 = 525. Add the carried over 7: 525 + 7 = 532. Write down 32, carry over 5.\n\nNext, the hundreds digit: 9.\n\n175 x 9 = 1,575. Add the carried over 5: 1,575 + 5 = 1,580. Write down 1,580.\n\nNow, add up the three partial products:\n\n700\n\n532\n\n1,580\n\nAdding 700 + 532 = 1,232. Then, 1,232 + 1,580 = 2,812. Wait, that's 2,812. But that's not 163,450. Wait, this is not matching. What's going on here?\n\nWait, no, hold on. Wait, in the vertical multiplication, the numbers being added are:\n\nFirst partial product: 700 (from 175 x 4)\n\nSecond partial product: 532 (from 175 x 30 + carried over 7)\n\nThird partial product: 1,580 (from 175 x 900)\n\nBut 700 + 532 + 1,580 = 700 + 532 = 1,232; 1,232 + 1,580 = 2,812. But that's only 2,812. Which is way too low. But that's impossible because we know the correct answer is 163,450. So, where is the mistake here?\n\nWait, no, actually, in the vertical multiplication, when you multiply by the tens digit (3), you have to multiply by 3 and then add a zero. So, 175 x 3 = 525, then add a zero: 5,250. But in the vertical layout, this is written as 525 shifted one position. So, when adding, you need to consider that 5,250 is in the tens place, so it's added as 525. Wait, but 5,250 is 5,250. If you shift it one position to the left, it becomes 525. So, adding 700 (from units) + 525 (from tens) + 15,750 (from hundreds). Wait, 700 + 525 = 1,225; 1,225 + 15,750 = 16,975. Wait, that's 16,975. Still not matching.\n\nWait, but according to the standard multiplication algorithm, the partial products should be:\n\n- 175 x 4 = 700\n\n- 175 x 30 = 5,250 (shifted one)\n\n- 175 x 900 = 15,750 (shifted two)\n\nAdding them together: 700 + 5,250 + 15,750 = 700 + 5,250 = 5,950; 5,950 + 15,750 = 21,700. But that's 21,700. Which is not matching the correct answer. So, something is wrong here.\n\nWait, but when I broke down 175 into