12,185. So the total product is 12,185. Wait, but let me verify this with another method to make sure.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use the distributive property. Let's see:\n\n819 x 429 can be broken down as 800 x 429 + 19 x 429. Let's compute each part.\n\nFirst, 800 x 429. 800 x 400 = 320,000. 800 x 29 = 23,200. So 320,000 + 23,200 = 343,200.\n\nThen, 19 x 429. 10 x 429 = 4,290. 9 x 429 = 3,861. So 4,290 + 3,861 = 8,151.\n\nNow, add 343,200 + 8,151. Let's do that:\n\n343,200\n+  8,151\n---------\n343,200 + 8,000 = 351,200\n351,200 + 151 = 351,351\n\nWait, that's different from the previous result. Wait, so now I have two different answers? That can't be. There must be a mistake here. Let me check both calculations again.\n\nFirst method: 819 x 429 = 7371 (ones place) + 1638 (tens) + 3276 (hundreds). Then adding those gives 12,185.\n\nSecond method: 800 x 429 = 343,200; 19 x 429 = 8,151. Adding those gives 343,200 + 8,151 = 351,351.\n\nThese two results are conflicting. That means I made a mistake somewhere. Let me check both methods again.\n\nFirst method:\n\nMultiplying 819 by 429:\n\nFirst partial product: 819 x 9 = 7,371. Correct.\n\nSecond partial product: 819 x 2 = 1,638. Correct.\n\nThird partial product: 819 x 4 = 3,276. Correct.\n\nAdding them up:\n\n7,371 + 1,638:\n\nLet me add 7,000 + 1,000 = 8,000\n\n300 + 600 = 900\n\n70 + 30 = 100\n\n1 + 8 = 9\n\nSo 8,000 + 900 = 8,900; 8,900 + 100 = 9,000; 9,000 + 9 = 9,009. Wait, hold on, this contradicts my previous result. Wait, no, wait. Wait, 7,371 + 1,638:\n\n7,371 + 1,000 = 8,371\n\n8,371 + 600 = 8,971\n\n8,971 + 30 = 8,971 + 30 = 9,001\n\n9,001 + 8 = 9,009. Oh! Wait, so my initial calculation was wrong. I thought 7,371 + 1,638 was 8,909, but actually, it's 9,009. Then adding 3,276 to 9,009:\n\n9,009 + 3,276:\n\n9,000 + 3,000 = 12,000\n\n0 + 200 = 200\n\n0 + 70 = 70\n\n9 + 6 = 15\n\nSo 12,000 + 200 = 12,200; 12,200 + 70 = 12,270; 12,270 + 15 = 12,285. Wait, that's different again. Now I'm confused. What's go