d 5,984 incorrectly. Instead, the correct way is to break it into 748\u00d7800 + 748\u00d790 + 748\u00d77, which gives 598,400 + 67,320 + 5,236 = 670,956. So that matches the first method. So the correct answer is 670,956.\n\nTherefore, my initial mistake in the standard multiplication was not breaking down the multiplication into the correct components. Instead, I should have multiplied by each place value separately and then added them up. So the correct product is 670,956.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 748 and 897 is \\boxed{670956}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 748 and 897, we can break down the multiplication using the distributive property:\n\n1. **Break down 748 into 700 + 48:**\n   - Calculate \\(700 \\times 897\\):\n     \\[\n     700 \\times 897 = 700 \\times (800 + 97) = 700 \\times 800 + 700 \\times 97 = 560000 + 67900 = 627900\n     \\]\n   - Calculate \\(48 \\times 897\\):\n     \\[\n     48 \\times 897 = (40 + 8) \\times 897 = 40 \\times 897 + 8 \\times 897\n     \\]\n     - Calculate \\(40 \\times 897\\):\n       \\[\n       40 \\times 897 = 40 \\times (800 + 97) = 40 \\times 800 + 40 \\times 97 = 32000 + 3880 = 35880\n       \\]\n     - Calculate \\(8 \\times 897\\):\n       \\[\n       8 \\times 897 = 8 \\times (800 + 97) = 8 \\times 800 + 8 \\times 97 = 6400 + 776 = 7176\n       \\]\n     - Add the results:\n       \\[\n       35880 + 7176 = 43056\n       \\]\n2. **Add the two parts together:**\n   - Add \\(627900\\) and \\(43056\\):\n     \\[\n     627900 + 43056 = 670956\n     \\]\n\nThus, the product of 748 and 897 is \\(\\boxed{670956}\\).",
