nFirst, 647*6=3,882.\n\nThen, 647*90. Since 596 is 596, which is 5*100 +9*10 +6. So 647*596=647*(5*100 +9*10 +6)=647*5*100 +647*9*10 +647*6.\n\nCompute each term:\n\n647*5=3,235. Then *100=323,500.\n\n647*9=5,823. Then *10=58,230.\n\n647*6=3,882.\n\nNow, add them all together: 323,500 +58,230 +3,882.\n\nFirst, 323,500 +58,230. 323,500 +50,000=373,500. 373,500 +8,230=381,730.\n\nThen add 3,882: 381,730 +3,882=385,612.\n\nYes! That's correct. So the answer is 385,612. \n\nSo the mistake in the earlier method was probably in how I was handling the partial products. By breaking down 596 into 500 +90 +6, it's much simpler. \n\nTherefore, the product of 647 and 596 is 385,612.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 647 and 596 is \\boxed{385612}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 647 and 596, we can break down 596 into its components: 500, 90, and 6. Then, we multiply 647 by each component and sum the results.\n\n1. Calculate \\( 647 \\times 6 \\):\n   \\[\n   647 \\times 6 = 3882\n   \\]\n\n2. Calculate \\( 647 \\times 90 \\):\n   \\[\n   647 \\times 90 = 647 \\times 9 \\times 10 = 5823 \\times 10 = 58230\n   \\]\n\n3. Calculate \\( 647 \\times 500 \\):\n   \\[\n   647 \\times 500 = 647 \\times 5 \\times 100 = 3235 \\times 100 = 323500\n   \\]\n\n4. Sum the results of the three components:\n   \\[\n   3882 + 58230 + 323500\n   \\]\n\n5. Add the first two results:\n   \\[\n   3882 + 58230 = 62112\n   \\]\n\n6. Add the third result to the sum:\n   \\[\n   62112 + 323500 = 385612\n   \\]\n\nThus, the product of 647 and 596 is \\(\\boxed{385612}\\).",
