      "text": "<think>\nOkay, so I need to find the product of 530 and 976. Hmm, let's see. I remember that multiplying two numbers can be done step by step, but maybe there's a quicker way to do it mentally. Let me think. \n\nFirst, maybe I can break down 530 into 500 + 30. That might make it easier to multiply by 976. So, if I have (500 + 30) times 976, I can use the distributive property. That means 500*976 + 30*976. Let me calculate each part separately.\n\nStarting with 500*976. Well, 500 is 5*100, so 5*976 is 4880, and then multiplied by 100 gives 488,000. Okay, that part seems straightforward. Now the other part: 30*976. Hmm, 30 is 3*10, so 3*976 would be... let's see. 3*900 is 2700, 3*70 is 210, and 3*6 is 18. Adding those together: 2700 + 210 is 2910, plus 18 is 2928. Then multiply by 10 gives 29,280. \n\nNow, add those two results together: 488,000 + 29,280. Let me add them step by step. 488,000 + 20,000 is 508,000. Then add 9,280: 508,000 + 9,280. 508,000 + 9,000 is 517,000, and then +280 is 517,280. So, is the product 517,280? Let me check my calculations again to make sure I didn't make a mistake.\n\nWait, let me verify the 30*976 again. 30 times 900 is 27,000. 30 times 70 is 2,100. 30 times 6 is 180. So adding those: 27,000 + 2,100 is 29,100, plus 180 is 29,280. Then multiplying by 10 gives 292,800. Wait, earlier I said 29,280 and then multiplied by 10 to get 292,800. Then adding to 488,000. So 488,000 + 292,800. Let's do that again. 488,000 + 200,000 is 688,000. Then add 92,800. 688,000 + 90,000 is 778,000. Then add 2,800: 778,000 + 2,800 is 780,800. Wait, that's different from before. Hmm, so where did I go wrong?\n\nWait, no. Wait, 30*976 is 29,280. Then 500*976 is 488,000. So adding 488,000 + 29,280. Let's do this another way. 488,000 + 29,280. Break down 29,280 into 20,000 + 9,000 + 280. So 488,000 + 20,000 = 508,000. Then 508,000 + 9,000 = 517,000. Then 517,000 + 280 = 517,280. Oh, right, so that's correct. So my initial calculation was right. Maybe I messed up when I thought of 30*976 as 292,800. Wait, no. 30*976 is 29,280. Then 29,280*10 is 292,800. Wait, no. Wait, 30*976 is 29,280. Then 500*976 is 488,000. So 488,000 + 29,280. Let me check 488,000 + 29,280. 488,000 + 20,000 is 508,000. Then 508,000 + 9,000 is 517,000. Then 517,000 + 280 is 517,280. Yes, that's correct. So the total is 517,280. \n\nAlternatively, maybe I can do the multiplication directly without breaking it down. Let's try that method to cross-verify. \n\nMultiplying 530 by 976. Let's do it step by step. \n\nFirst, multiply 530 by 6. That's 3,180. \n\nThen multiply 530 by 70. 530*70. 530*7 is 3,710. Then add a zero: 37,100. \n\nThen multiply 530 by 900. 530*9 is 4,770. Then add two zeros: 477,000. \n\nNow add all three results together: 3,180 + 37,100 + 477,000. \n\nFirst, 3,180 + 37,100. 3,000 + 37,000 is 40,000. 180 + 100 is 280. So total is 40,280. Then add 477,000. 40,280 + 477,000. 40,000 + 477,000 is 517,000. Then add the remaining 280: 517,000 + 280 = 517,280. \n\nOkay, same result. So that's good. So both methods give 517,280. So that must be the correct answer. \n\nAlternatively, maybe use another method. Let's see. 530 * 976. Let's write it out vertically:\n\n    530\n  x 976\n  ------\n    3,180  (530 x 6)\n   47,100   (530 x 70)\n  477,000    (530 x 900)\n  ------\n    517,280\n\nAdding those up: 3,180 + 47,100 = 50,280. Then 50,280 + 477,000 = 517,280. Yep, same answer. \n\nSo, all methods lead to 517,280. Therefore, the product of 530 and 976 is 517,280. \n\nI think that's solid. Let me just check with a calculator to be absolutely sure. Well, since I don't have a calculator here, but I can cross-verify with another multiplication approach. \n\nAlternatively, maybe use the fact that 976 is 1000 - 24. So 530*(1000 - 24) = 530,000 - (530*24). Let's compute 530*24. 500*24 = 12,000. 30*24 = 720. So total is 12,000 + 720 = 12,720. Then subtract from 530,000: 530,000 - 12,720 = 517,280. \n\nOh, that's another way to do it. So that also gives 517,280. So all methods converge to the same answer. Therefore, I can be confident that the product is 517,280.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 530 and 976 is \\boxed{517280}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 530 and 976, we can use the distributive property:\n\n1. Break down 530 into 500 + 30.\n2. Calculate each part separately:\n   - \\(500 \\times 976 = 488,000\\)\n   - \\(30 \\times 976 = 29,280\\)\n3. Add the results together:\n   - \\(488,000 + 29,280 = 517,280\\)\n\nVerification using another method:\n1. Multiply 530 by each digit of 976 and sum the results:\n   - \\(530 \\times 6 = 3,180\\)\n   - \\(530 \\times 70 = 37,100\\)\n   - \\(530 \\times 900 = 477,000\\)\n2. Add the results:\n   - \\(3,180 + 37,100 + 477,000 = 517,280\\)\n\nVerification using the difference of squares:\n1. \\(976 = 1000 - 24\\)\n2. Calculate \\(530 \\times 976 = 530 \\times (1000 - 24) = 530,000 - (530 \\times 24)\\)\n3. Calculate \\(530 \\times 24 = 12,720\\)\n4. Subtract from 530,000: \\(530,000 - 12,720 = 517,280\\)\n\nAll methods confirm the product of 530 and 976 is \\(\\boxed{517280}\\).",
