igits gives 56,600. Correct.\n\nMultiplication by 4: 566 \u00d7 4 = 2,264. Shifting left one digit gives 22,640. Correct.\n\nSo, adding 22,640 + 56,600 + 113,200. Let's do this again:\n\n22,640 + 56,600. 22,640 + 50,000 = 72,640. 72,640 + 6,600 = 79,240. Then, 79,240 + 113,200. 79,240 + 100,000 = 179,240. 179,240 + 13,200 = 192,440. So, total is 192,440. But according to the distributive method, it's 121,124. Which is correct?\n\nWait, now I'm really confused. There must be a mistake in one of the methods. Let me check with another approach. Let's compute 566 \u00d7 214 using the standard algorithm step by step.\n\nMultiplying 566 by 214:\n\nFirst, write 566  \n\u00d7\u00a0\u00a0214  \n________\n\nMultiply 566 by 4 (ones digit):\n\n4  \n\u00d7\u00a0566  \n________  \n224  \nSo, 224. Since it's the ones place, write 224 and move on. But wait, 4 \u00d7 566 is 2264. So, why is it 224? Because when you multiply 4 by 566, you get 2264, but since it's the ones digit, you write 2264 and then shift left by one digit, making it 22640. So, that's correct.\n\nThen, multiply 566 by 1 (tens digit):\n\n1  \n\u00d7\u00a0566  \n________  \n566  \nSince it's the tens place, write 566 and shift two digits left, making it 56600. Correct.\n\nMultiply 566 by 2 (hundreds digit):\n\n2  \n\u00d7\u00a0566  \n________  \n1,132  \nSince it's the hundreds place, write 1,132 and shift three digits left, making it 113,200. Correct.\n\nNow, adding the three partial products:\n\n22,640 (from 4\u00d7566 shifted)  \n+56,600 (from 1\u00d7566 shifted)  \n+113,200 (from 2\u00d7566 shifted)  \n= ?\n\nLet's add them step by step:\n\nFirst, 22,640 + 56,600.  \n22,640 + 50,000 = 72,640  \n72,640 + 6,600 = 79,240\n\nThen, 79,240 + 113,200.  \n79,240 + 100,000 = 179,240  \n179,240 + 13,200 = 192,440\n\nSo, total is 192,440. But according to the distributive method, it's 121,124. Which is correct?\n\nWait, now I'm really confused. Let me check with another method. Let's compute 566 \u00d7 214 by breaking down