 when you multiply by the units digit, you get a three-digit number, so you write it down as is. Then multiplying by the tens digit (9) would be a three-digit number shifted left by one digit (i.e., multiplied by 10), and multiplying by the hundreds digit (6) would be a three-digit number shifted left by two digits (i.e., multiplied by 100). Then you add them all together.\n\nSo, let's do it step by step:\n\nFirst, multiply 967 by 2 (units digit):\n\n967 * 2 = 1934. Write down 1934.\n\nNext, multiply 967 by 9 (tens digit), which is 8703. Since this is the tens digit, we need to shift it left by one digit (multiply by 10):\n\n8703 * 10 = 87,030. So write down 87,030.\n\nThen, multiply 967 by 6 (hundreds digit), which is 5,802. Since this is the hundreds digit, shift left by two digits (multiply by 100):\n\n5,802 * 100 = 58,0200. Wait, that's 58,020 multiplied by 10? Wait, no. Wait, shifting left by two digits is multiplying by 100. So 5,802 * 100 = 58,0200? Wait, 5,802 * 100 is 58,020. Wait, 5,802 * 10 is 58,020. So yes, shifting left by two digits would be multiplying by 100. So 58,020.\n\nNow, add them all together:\n\n1934\n\n+87,030\n\n+58,020\n\nLet's add 1934 and 87,030 first:\n\n1934 + 87,030 = 88,964\n\nThen add 58,020:\n\n88,964 + 58,020 = 146,984\n\nWait, that's different from the previous result. Hmm, so now I have two different answers: 669,164 and 146,984. That can't be right. There must be a mistake here.\n\nWait, hold on. When I did the first method, expanding (1000 - 33)(700 - 8), I got 669,164. Then when I did the standard multiplication step by step, I got 146,984. These are conflicting. Which one is correct?\n\nWait, maybe I messed up the standard multiplication method. Let me check again.\n\nWait, in the standard multiplication, when you multiply by the hundreds digit, you have to shift left by two digits. So 967 * 6 = 5,802. Then, since it's the hundreds place, you multiply by 100, so 5,802 * 100 = 58,020. Then, adding that to the previous partial products.\n\nBut 967 * 692 is 967*(700 - 8) = 967*700 - 967*8. Let's compute that.\n\n967*700: 967*7*100. 967*7: 6,769. So 6,769*100 = 676,900.\n\n967*8: 7,736.\n\nSo 676,900 - 7,736 = 669,164. Which matches the first method. So why does the standard multiplication give me 146,984? Because I must have messed up the alignment.\n\nWait, in the standard multiplication, when you do 967*692, you have to consider that 692 is 6*100 + 9*10 + 2*1. So the partial products should be:\n\n967*2 (units) = 1934\n\n967*9 (tens) = 8703, shifted left by one (so 87030)\n\n967*6 (hundreds) = 5802, shifted left by two (so 580200)\n\nThen adding them:\n\n1934\n\n+87030\n\n+580200\n\nLet's compute that:\n\nFirst, 1934 + 87030 = 88,964\n\nThen 88,964 + 580,200 = 669,164. Ah! There we go. I must have added the numbers incorrectly earlier.\n\nYes, 88,964 + 580,200. Let's do 88,964 + 580,200. 88,964 + 500,000 = 588,964. Then 58,200 more: 588,964 + 58,200 = 647,164. Wait, that's not right. Wait, 580,200 is 500,000 + 80,200. So 88,964 + 500,000 = 588,964. Then 588,964 + 80,200 = 669,164. Yes, that's correct. So the standard multiplication actually gives 669,164 when done properly. So my initial mistake was adding the numbers incorrectly. So both methods give the same result, 669,164. Therefore, the correct answer is 669,164.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can check using another method. Let's try using the difference of squares or something else. Wait, 967 and 692. Hmm, not sure. Alternatively, maybe approximate.\n\n967 is approximately 1000, and 692 is approximately 700. So 1000*700 = 700,000. The actual answer is 669,164, which is 30,836 less than 700,000. That seems reasonable.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the calculator method. But since I don't have a calculator, perhaps another check.\n\nLet me compute 967*692 using another decomposition. Let's write 692 as 700 - 8. Then 967*(700 - 8) = 967*700 - 967*8. As before, 967*700 is 676,900. 967*8 is 7,736. Then 676,900 - 7,736 = 669,164. Yep, same result.\n\nAlternatively, maybe check with another multiplication. Let's take 967*692. Let's do 967*700 = 676,900. Then subtract 967*8 = 7,736. So 676,900 - 7,736. Let's compute 676,900 - 7,000 = 669,900. Then subtract 736: 669,900 - 736 = 669,164. Correct.\n\nTherefore, all methods lead to 669,164. So I think that's the correct answer.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 967 and 692 is \\boxed{669164}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 967 and 692, we can use the distributive property:\n\n\\[\n967 \\times 692 = (1000 - 33) \\times (700 - 8)\n\\]\n\nExpanding this expression:\n\n\\[\n(1000 - 33) \\times (700 - 8) = 1000 \\times 700 + 1000 \\times (-8) + (-33) \\times 700 + (-33) \\times (-8)\n\\]\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n\\[\n1000 \\times 700 = 700,000\n\\]\n\\[\n1000 \\times (-8) = -8,000\n\\]\n\\[\n-33 \\times 700 = -23,100\n\\]\n\\[\n-33 \\times (-8) = 264\n\\]\n\nAdding these results together:\n\n\\[\n700,000 - 8,000 - 23,100 + 264\n\\]\n\nFirst, subtract 8,000 from 700,000:\n\n\\[\n700,000 - 8,000 = 692,000\n\\]\n\nNext, subtract 23,100 from 692,000:\n\n\\[\n692,000 - 23,100 = 668,900\n\\]\n\nFinally, add 264 to 668,900:\n\n\\[\n668,900 + 264 = 669,164\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 967 and 692 is \\(\\boxed{669164}\\).",
