n 328*36 is 11,808. Wait, wait, 328*36. Let me compute that again. 328*30=9,840 and 328*6=1,968. So 9,840 + 1,968 = 11,808. Then 196,800 + 11,808 = 208,608. Oh, right! So I must have miscalculated 28*36 earlier. Wait, 28*36. Let me check that again. 28*36. 20*36=720, 8*36=288. 720+288=1,008. So that's correct. So 328*36=11,808. Then 328*600=196,800. So total is 196,800 + 11,808 = 208,608. So that's correct. So my initial mistake was when I first thought 28*36 was 1,008, but actually, 28*36 is 1,008. Wait, no, 28*36 is 1,008? Wait, 28*36. Let me compute 28*36. 28*30=840, 28*6=168. 840+168=1,008. Yes, that's correct. So 328*36=11,808. Then 328*600=196,800. So 196,800 + 11,808 = 208,608. So that's correct. So the first method actually does give the same answer as the standard multiplication method. So the answer is 208,608.\n\nBut let me confirm with another method. Let's use the distributive property differently. 328*636. Let's write 636 as (600 + 30 + 6). So 328*(600 + 30 + 6) = 328*600 + 328*30 + 328*6. Which is 196,800 + 9,840 + 1,968. Adding those together: 196,800 + 9,840 = 206,640; 206,640 + 1,968 = 208,608. Same result. So that's consistent.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using a calculator to verify. But since I don't have a calculator here, let's try another way. Let's compute 328*636.\n\nAlternatively, note that 328*636 = (300 + 28)*(600 + 36). Wait, that's the same as before. Alternatively, maybe use the difference of squares or something, but that might complicate. Alternatively, 328*636. Let's compute 328*600 = 196,800; 328*36 = 11,808; sum them. As before.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use 328*636 = 328*(600 + 36) = 328*600 + 328*36. Which is 196,800 + 11,808 = 208,608. So same answer.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use 328*636 = (300 + 28)*(600 + 36) = 300*600 + 300*36 + 28*600 + 28*36. Which is 180,000 + 10,800 + 16,800 + 1,008. Which is 180,000 + 10,800 = 190,800; 190,800 + 16,800 = 207,600; 207,600 + 1,008 = 208,608. So same result.\n\nTherefore, all methods lead to 208,608. So the product of 328 and 636 is 208,608. Therefore, the answer should be 208,608.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 328 and 636 is \\boxed{208608}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 328 and 636, we can break down the numbers and use the distributive property:\n\n1. Break down 328 into 300 + 28 and 636 into 600 + 36.\n2. Multiply each part separately:\n   - \\(300 \\times 600 = 180,000\\)\n   - \\(300 \\times 36 = 10,800\\)\n   - \\(28 \\times 600 = 16,800\\)\n   - \\(28 \\times 36 = 1,008\\)\n3. Sum the results of each multiplication:\n   - \\(180,000 + 10,800 = 190,800\\)\n   - \\(190,800 + 16,800 = 207,600\\)\n   - \\(207,600 + 1,008 = 208,608\\)\n\nWe can also verify this using the standard multiplication algorithm:\n1. Multiply 328 by 6 (units place): \\(328 \\times 6 = 1,968\\)\n2. Multiply 328 by 30 (tens place): \\(328 \\times 3 = 984\\), shifted one position left: \\(9,840\\)\n3. Multiply 328 by 600 (hundreds place): \\(328 \\times 6 = 1,968\\), shifted two positions left: \\(196,800\\)\n4. Sum the results:\n   - \\(196,800 + 9,840 = 206,640\\)\n   - \\(206,640 + 1,968 = 208,608\\)\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 328 and 636 is \\(\\boxed{208608}\\).",
