is can't be. There's a confusion here. Wait, no. Wait, in the vertical multiplication, the third partial product is 839 shifted two places left, which is 83,900, not 839. So, the third partial product should be 83,900, not 839. Therefore, when adding, it's 1678 + 2517 + 83,900.\n\nSo, 1678 + 2517 = 4195. Then, 4195 + 83,900. Let's compute 4,195 + 83,900. 4,000 + 83,000 = 87,000. 195 + 900 = 1,095. So, 87,000 + 1,095 = 88,095. Wait, that's not 110,748. Wait, now I'm really confused. What's happening here.\n\nWait, no. Wait, 83,900 is 83,900. So, 4,195 + 83,900. Let's do 4,000 + 83,000 = 87,000. Then, 195 + 900 = 1,095. So, 87,000 + 1,095 = 88,095. But that's not matching the previous total. Wait, but 839*100 is 83,900. So, adding 1678 + 25,170 + 83,900. Let's compute 1678 + 25,170 first. 1,678 + 25,170. 1,000 + 25,000 = 26,000. 678 + 170 = 848. So, 26,000 + 848 = 26,848. Then, 26,848 + 83,900. 20,000 + 80,000 = 100,000. 6,848 + 3,900 = 10,748. Then, 100,000 + 10,748 = 110,748. There we go. So, that's correct. So, the confusion was because I was mistakenly adding 839 instead of 83,900. So, the vertical multiplication method does give 110,748 when done correctly.\n\nTherefore, both methods confirm that the product of 839 and 132 is 110,748. So, the correct answer is 110,748.\n\nBut just to be absolutely thorough, let me try multiplying 839 by 132 using another approach. Let's use the fact that 132 is 12*11. So, 839*12*11. Maybe that's easier? Let's see.\n\nFirst, compute 839*12. Then, multiply the result by 11.\n\nCalculating 839*12:\n\nBreak down 12 into 10 + 2.\n\n839*10 = 8,390.\n\n839*2 = 1,678.\n\nAdding them together: 8,390 + 1,678. Let's compute 8,000 + 1,000 = 9,000. 390 + 678 = 1,068. Then, 9,000 + 1,068 = 10,068. So, 839*12 = 10,068.\n\nNow, multiply 10,068 by 11. Let's do that.\n\n10,068*11. Break it down into 10,068*10 + 10,068*1.\n\n10,068*10 = 100,680.\n\n10,068*1 = 10,068.\n\nAdding them: 100,680 + 10,068. Let's compute 100,000 + 10,000 = 110,000. 680 + 68 = 748. So, 110,000 + 748 = 110,748. Again, the same result. So, this method also gives 110,748. Therefore, all methods converge to the same answer. So, I can be confident that the product of 839 and 132 is 110,748.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is 110,748.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 839 and 132 is \\boxed{110748}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 839 and 132, we can use the distributive property by breaking down 132 into 100 + 30 + 2. \n\n1. Calculate each part separately:\n   - \\( 839 \\times 100 = 83900 \\)\n   - \\( 839 \\times 30 = 25170 \\)\n   - \\( 839 \\times 2 = 1678 \\)\n\n2. Add the results together:\n   - First, add \\( 83900 \\) and \\( 25170 \\):\n     \\[\n     83900 + 25170 = 109070\n     \\]\n   - Then, add the result to \\( 1678 \\):\n     \\[\n     109070 + 1678 = 110748\n     \\]\n\nVerification using another method (vertical multiplication) confirms the result:\n- Multiply 839 by 2, 30, and 100 (shifted appropriately) and sum the results:\n  \\[\n  \\begin{array}{r}\n    839 \\\\\n  \\times 132 \\\\\n  \\hline\n   1678 \\quad (\\text{839} \\times 2) \\\\\n  25170 \\quad (\\text{839} \\times 30 \\text{ shifted one position}) \\\\\n  83900 \\quad (\\text{839} \\times 100 \\text{ shifted two positions}) \\\\\n  \\hline\n  110748 \\quad (\\text{sum of the partial products})\n  \\end{array}\n  \\]\n\nThus, the product of 839 and 132 is \\(\\boxed{110748}\\).",
