ng. So that's corrected now.\n\nSo, all methods lead to 89,604. Therefore, the product of 786 and 114 is 89,604.\n\nBut just to be absolutely sure, let me do the multiplication using another method. Let's use the standard algorithm step by step.\n\nMultiplying 786 by 114:\n\nFirst, write 786 x 114.\n\nStart with the ones digit of the multiplier, which is 4. Multiply 786 by 4:\n\n786\nx  4\n-----\n3144\n\nThen multiply 786 by the tens digit, which is 1. Since it's in the tens place, the result is 7860, but we add a zero at the end:\n\n   786\nx  114\n-------\n  3144  (786 x 4)\n+7860   (786 x 10, shifted one position to the left)\n+78600  (786 x 100, shifted two positions to the left)\n----------\nAdding these up:\n\nFirst, 3144 + 7860. Let's compute that:\n\n3144\n+7860\n=11,004\n\nThen add 78,600:\n\n11,004\n+78,600\n=89,604\n\nYes, that's the same result. So all methods confirm that the product is 89,604. Therefore, I can be confident that this is the correct answer.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 786 and 114 is \\boxed{89604}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 786 and 114, we can use the distributive property:\n\n1. Break down 114 into 100 + 10 + 4.\n2. Multiply 786 by each component and then sum the results.\n\nFirst, multiply 786 by 4:\n\\[\n786 \\times 4 = 3144\n\\]\n\nNext, multiply 786 by 10:\n\\[\n786 \\times 10 = 7860\n\\]\n\nThen, multiply 786 by 100:\n\\[\n786 \\times 100 = 78600\n\\]\n\nAdd the results together:\n\\[\n3144 + 7860 + 78600\n\\]\n\nFirst, add 3144 and 7860:\n\\[\n3144 + 7860 = 11004\n\\]\n\nThen, add the result to 78600:\n\\[\n11004 + 78600 = 89604\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 786 and 114 is \\(\\boxed{89604}\\).",
