rst, multiply 442 by 200. That's 442*2*100. 442*2 is 884, so 884*100 is 88,400.\n\nThen multiply 442 by 3. That's 1,326.\n\nAdd 88,400 and 1,326. 88,400 + 1,000 is 89,400. Then 89,400 + 326 is 89,726. Yep, same result.\n\nSo all methods lead to 89,726. Therefore, the product of 442 and 203 is 89,726.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 442 and 203 is \\boxed{89726}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 442 and 203, we can use the distributive property. First, decompose 203 into 200 + 3. Then, multiply 442 by each part and add the results:\n\n1. Calculate \\( 442 \\times 3 \\):\n   \\[\n   442 \\times 3 = 1326\n   \\]\n\n2. Calculate \\( 442 \\times 200 \\):\n   \\[\n   442 \\times 200 = 88400\n   \\]\n\n3. Add the results of \\( 442 \\times 200 \\) and \\( 442 \\times 3 \\):\n   \\[\n   88400 + 1326 = 89726\n   \\]\n\nThus, the product of 442 and 203 is \\(\\boxed{89726}\\).",
