63}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 737 and 599, we can use the distributive property. Here are the key steps:\n\n1. **Break down the multiplication using the distributive property:**\n   \\[\n   737 \\times 599 = 737 \\times (600 - 1) = 737 \\times 600 - 737 \\times 1\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate each part separately:**\n   - Calculate \\(737 \\times 600\\):\n     \\[\n     737 \\times 600 = 737 \\times 6 \\times 100 = 4422 \\times 100 = 442200\n     \\]\n   - Calculate \\(737 \\times 1\\):\n     \\[\n     737 \\times 1 = 737\n     \\]\n\n3. **Subtract the second result from the first:**\n   \\[\n   442200 - 737 = 441463\n   \\]\n\n4. **Verification using another method (standard multiplication):**\n   - Multiply 737 by 9 (units digit of 599):\n     \\[\n     737 \\times 9 = 6633\n     \\]\n   - Multiply 737 by 90 (tens digit of 599):\n     \\[\n     737 \\times 90 = 6633 \\times 10 = 66330\n     \\]\n   - Multiply 737 by 500 (hundreds digit of 599):\n     \\[\n     737 \\times 500 = 368500\n     \\]\n   - Add all results together:\n     \\[\n     6633 + 66330 + 368500 = 441463\n     \\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 737 and 599 is \\(\\boxed{441463}\\).",
