-\n       4,780  (896 x 5)\n      8,360   (896 x 6, shifted one position to the left)\n     8,960    (896 x 1, shifted two positions to the left)\n     ------\n       147,840\n\nAdding those up: 4,780 + 8,360 = 13,140. Then 13,140 + 8,960 = 22,100. Wait, that doesn't match. Wait, no, hold on. Wait, in the standard multiplication, the first line is 896 x 5 = 4,480. Then the next line is 896 x 60 = 53,760, shifted one position to the left (so it's 5,3760?), and the third line is 896 x 100 = 89,600, shifted two positions to the left (896,000). Then adding them up:\n\n4,480\n+53,760\n+89,600\n--------\nLet's add 4,480 + 53,760 first. 4,000 + 53,000 = 57,000. 480 + 760 = 1,240. So total is 57,000 + 1,240 = 58,240. Then add 89,600: 58,240 + 89,600. 50,000 + 80,000 = 130,000. 8,240 + 9,600 = 17,840. So 130,000 + 17,840 = 147,840. There we go. So that matches the previous result. So 147,840. So that seems correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use distributive property differently. Let's see, 165 is 170 - 5. So 896*(170 - 5) = 896*170 - 896*5. Let's compute that.\n\nFirst, 896*170. 170 is 100 + 70. So 896*100=89,600; 896*70=62,720. So 89,600 + 62,720 = 152,320. Then subtract 896*5=4,480. So 152,320 - 4,480. Let's compute that. 152,320 - 4,000 = 148,320. Then subtract 480: 148,320 - 480 = 147,840. Again, same result. So that's a good check.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use another decomposition. Let's see, 165 is 100 + 60 + 5. Wait, that's what I did first. So all methods lead to 147,840. So I think that's the correct answer.\n\nWait, just to make sure, maybe do a quick check with another method. Let's use the fact that 896 is 900 - 4. So 900*165 = 148,500. Then subtract 4*165=660. So 148,500 - 660 = 147,840. Yep, same answer. So that's another way to confirm.\n\nSo all different methods give me 147,840. So I think that's the right answer. Therefore, the product of 896 and 165 is 147,840.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 896 and 165 is \\boxed{147840}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 896 and 165, we can break down 165 into 100, 60, and 5, and then multiply each part by 896 and sum the results:\n\n1. Calculate \\( 896 \\times 100 \\):\n   \\[\n   896 \\times 100 = 89600\n   \\]\n\n2. Calculate \\( 896 \\times 60 \\):\n   \\[\n   896 \\times 60 = 53760\n   \\]\n\n3. Calculate \\( 896 \\times 5 \\):\n   \\[\n   896 \\times 5 = 4480\n   \\]\n\n4. Add the results together:\n   \\[\n   89600 + 53760 + 4480\n   \\]\n\n   First, add \\( 89600 \\) and \\( 53760 \\):\n   \\[\n   89600 + 53760 = 143360\n   \\]\n\n   Then, add the remaining result:\n   \\[\n   143360 + 4480 = 147840\n   \\]\n\nVerification using different methods (such as the distributive property, breaking down 165 into 170 - 5, or using the standard multiplication algorithm) confirms the result. All methods lead to the same final answer.\n\nThe product of 896 and 165 is \\(\\boxed{147840}\\).",
