= 10 \u2192 0, carry 1\n\n6 + 9 = 15 + 1 = 16 \u2192 6, carry 1\n\n4 + 4 = 8 + 1 = 9\n\nSo total is 69,600. Then add 835,200:\n\n69,600 + 835,200:\n\nStart from the right:\n\n0 + 0 = 0\n\n0 + 2 = 2\n\n6 + 5 = 11 \u2192 1, carry 1\n\n9 + 3 + 1 = 13 \u2192 3, carry 1\n\n6 + 8 = 14 + 1 = 15 \u2192 5, carry 1\n\n0 + 0 + 1 = 1\n\nWait, but 69,600 is 6 (ten-thousands), 9 (thousands), 6 (hundreds), 0 (tens), 0 (ones). 835,200 is 8 (hundred-thousands), 3 (ten-thousands), 5 (thousands), 2 (hundreds), 0 (tens), 0 (ones). So adding:\n\n69,600 + 835,200:\n\n6 (ten-thousands) + 8 (hundred-thousands) = 14 \u2192 4, carry 1\n\n9 (thousands) + 3 (ten-thousands) + 1 (carry) = 13 \u2192 3, carry 1\n\n6 (hundreds) + 5 (thousands) + 1 (carry) = 12 \u2192 2, carry 1\n\n0 (tens) + 2 (hundreds) + 1 (carry) = 3\n\n0 (ones) + 0 = 0\n\nWait, this is confusing. Let me write them as numbers:\n\n69,600 is 069,600\n\n835,200 is 835,200\n\nAdding them:\n\n069,600\n\n+835,200\n\n= 904,800. Ah! There we go. So when adding 69,600 + 835,200, the correct sum is 904,800. So my initial mistake was in the first method's addition where I thought the sum was 951,720, but actually, it's 904,800. So the correct answer is 904,800.\n\nTherefore, the product of 928 and 975 is 904,800. Let me confirm once more with another method. Let's use the distributive property again.\n\n928 \u00d7 975 = 928 \u00d7 (900 + 70 + 5) = 928\u00d7900 + 928\u00d770 + 928\u00d75 = 835,200 + 64,960 + 4,640. Adding those gives 835,200 + 64,960 = 900,160; 900,160 + 4,640 = 904,800. Correct.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is 904,800. My initial addition in the first method had a mistake in the way I was adding the digits, leading me to an incorrect result. After correcting that, all methods agree on 904,800.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 928 and 975 is \\boxed{904800}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 928 and 975, we can use the distributive property:\n\n\\[\n928 \\times 975 = 928 \\times (900 + 70 + 5)\n\\]\n\nFirst, calculate each component separately:\n\n1. \\( 928 \\times 900 \\):\n   \\[\n   928 \\times 9 = 8352 \\implies 928 \\times 900 = 8352 \\times 100 = 835200\n   \\]\n\n2. \\( 928 \\times 70 \\):\n   \\[\n   928 \\times 7 = 6496 \\implies 928 \\times 70 = 6496 \\times 10 = 64960\n   \\]\n\n3. \\( 928 \\times 5 \\):\n   \\[\n   928 \\times 5 = 4640\n   \\]\n\nNext, add the results together:\n\n\\[\n835200 + 64960 + 4640\n\\]\n\nStart by adding the first two products:\n\n\\[\n835200 + 64960 = 900160\n\\]\n\nThen add the third product:\n\n\\[\n900160 + 4640 = 904800\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 928 and 975 is \\(\\boxed{904800}\\).",
