om the rightmost digit:\n\n4 (from 744)\n\n6 (from 29760) \u2192 4 + 6 = 10, carry over 1.\n\nNext digit: 8 (from 744) and 0 (from 29760) \u2192 8 + 0 = 8, plus the carried 1 is 9.\n\nNext digit: 7 (from 744) and 7 (from 29760) \u2192 7 + 7 = 14, plus 0 (since 595200 has a 0 here) \u2192 14. Wait, but 595200 is 5 9 5 2 0 0. So when aligned properly:\n\nWait, maybe I need to write them with the same number of digits:\n\n744 is 0 0 744\n\n29760 is 0 29760 (but 29760 is 5 digits: 2 9 7 6 0)\n\n595200 is 595200 (6 digits: 5 9 5 2 0 0)\n\nSo when adding:\n\n      0 0 744\n\n    0 2 9 7 6 0\n\n  + 5 9 5 2 0 0\n\nStart from the right:\n\nOnes place: 4 + 0 + 0 = 4.\n\nTens place: 8 + 6 + 0 = 14. Write 4, carry 1.\n\nHundreds place: 7 + 7 + 0 = 14, plus carried 1 = 15. Write 5, carry 1.\n\nThousands place: 9 + 9 + 0 = 18, plus carried 1 = 19. Write 9, carry 1.\n\nTen-thousands place: 0 + 2 + 0 = 2, plus carried 1 = 3. Write 3, carry 0.\n\nHundred-thousands place: 0 + 5 + 0 = 5.\n\nSo the total is 5 3 9 5 4. Wait, that's 53954? But that doesn't make sense. Wait, no, let's check again.\n\nWait, the numbers being added are:\n\nFirst number: 744 (three digits)\n\nSecond number: 29760 (five digits)\n\nThird number: 595200 (six digits)\n\nTo add them, we need to align them properly:\n\n      00744\n\n    029760\n\n  +595200\n\nNow, adding digit by digit:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n4 (units place)\n\n6 (tens place) + 4 (from first number's tens place) = 10? Wait, no. Wait, the first number is 00744, which is 744. So when written as:\n\n      0 0 7 4 4\n\nThe digits are:\n\nPosition 5: 0\n\nPosition 4: 0\n\nPosition 3: 7\n\nPosition 2: 4\n\nPosition 1: 4\n\nSimilarly, 029760 is:\n\nPosition 5: 0\n\nPosition 4: 2\n\nPosition 3: 9\n\nPosition 2: 7\n\nPosition 1: 6\n\nPosition 0: 0\n\nAnd 595200 is:\n\nPosition 5: 5\n\nPosition 4: 9\n\nPosition 3: 5\n\nPosition 2: 2\n\nPosition 1: 0\n\nPosition 0: 0\n\nSo adding:\n\nPosition 0 (units): 4 (from 744) + 6 (from 29760) + 0 (from 595200