yover 6. So 1,376 + 6 = 1,382.\n\nPutting it all together: 1,382 followed by 8 and 0. So 144,480. Exactly the same result. So that's another confirmation.\n\nTherefore, regardless of the method used, the product of 344 and 420 is 144,480. I think that's solid. I don't see any mistakes in my calculations, and multiple methods cross-check the result. So I'm confident that's the correct answer.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 344 and 420 is \\boxed{144480}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 344 and 420, we can break down the numbers and use the distributive property:\n\n1. Break down 344 into 300, 40, and 4.\n2. Break down 420 into 400, 20, and 0.\n\nMultiply each component separately and then sum the results:\n\n- \\( 300 \\times 400 = 120,000 \\)\n- \\( 300 \\times 20 = 6,000 \\)\n- \\( 40 \\times 400 = 16,000 \\)\n- \\( 40 \\times 20 = 800 \\)\n- \\( 4 \\times 400 = 1,600 \\)\n- \\( 4 \\times 20 = 80 \\)\n\nAdding these products together:\n\n\\[\n120,000 + 6,000 + 16,000 + 800 + 1,600 + 80 = 144,480\n\\]\n\nVerification using the standard multiplication algorithm confirms the result. Additionally, breaking down 420 into 500 - 80 and using the distributive property also yields the same result.\n\nThus, the product of 344 and 420 is \\(\\boxed{144480}\\).",
