e third partial product (for 900) is shifted two positions left, so 4995 becomes 499500. Then adding all three partial products: 555 + 38850 + 499500 = 538,905. So that's correct.\n\nBut in my second calculation, when I thought of multiplying by 900, 70, 1, I added 555 + 38850 + 49950, which is 555 + 38850 is 394,055 + 49,950 is 434,005. Wait, that's wrong. Wait, why?\n\nAh! Because when you multiply by 971, the partial products are:\n\n- 555 x 1 = 555 (units place)\n- 555 x 70 = 38,850 (tens and hundreds place)\n- 555 x 900 = 499,500 (thousands, ten thousands, hundred thousands place)\n\nSo when adding, you need to align them properly:\n\n   555\n  x 971\n  ------\n   555  (555 x 1)\n  3885  (555 x 70, shifted one left)\n 49950  (555 x 900, shifted two left)\n  ------\n 538905\n\nSo adding 555 + 3885 + 49950. Wait, but 3885 is 3,885 and 49950 is 49,950. So 555 + 3,885 = 4,440; 4,440 + 49,950 = 54,390. Wait, that's not matching either. Wait, no, this is confusing.\n\nWait, no. Wait, in the standard multiplication, the partial products are:\n\n- The first partial product is 555 (from multiplying by the units digit 1)\n- The second partial product is 3885 shifted one position left (so it's 38850)\n- The third partial product is 4995 shifted two positions left (so it's 499500)\n\nTherefore, adding them together: 555 + 38850 + 499500. Let's compute that:\n\nFirst, 555 + 38850 = 394,055\n\nThen, 394,055 + 499,500 = 538,905. Yes, that's correct.\n\nEarlier, when I thought of multiplying by 900, 70, 1, I added 555 + 38850 + 49950, which is wrong because 49950 is actually 4995 shifted two left, which is 499500. So I must have misaligned the numbers. So the correct way is to add 555 + 38850 + 499500, which gives 538,905. So both methods agree. Therefore, the answer is 538,905.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can check using a calculator. But since I don't have a calculator here, let me try another way. Let's use the fact that 555 * 971 = 555*(1000 - 29) = 555*1000 - 555*29. Let's 