efore, the product of 746 and 536 is 399,856.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 746 and 536 is \\boxed{399856}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 746 and 536, we use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. Multiply 746 by each digit of 536, starting from the rightmost digit (6), then the middle digit (3), and finally the leftmost digit (5). Each subsequent multiplication is shifted one place to the left.\n\n   - Multiply 746 by 6:\n     \\[\n     746 \\times 6 = 4476\n     \\]\n   - Multiply 746 by 3 (shifted one place to the left):\n     \\[\n     746 \\times 3 = 2238 \\quad \\text{(shifted left by 1)} \\quad 22380\n     \\]\n   - Multiply 746 by 5 (shifted two places to the left):\n     \\[\n     746 \\times 5 = 3730 \\quad \\text{(shifted left by 2)} \\quad 373000\n     \\]\n\n2. Add the results of the three multiplications:\n   \\[\n   4476 + 22380 + 373000\n   \\]\n\n3. Perform the addition step-by-step:\n   - First, add 4476 and 22380:\n     \\[\n     4476 + 22380 = 26856\n     \\]\n   - Then, add the result to 373000:\n     \\[\n     26856 + 373000 = 399856\n     \\]\n\nThus, the product of 746 and 536 is \\(\\boxed{399856}\\).",
