and 373 is \\boxed{68259}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 183 and 373, we can use the distributive property:\n\n\\[\n183 \\times 373 = (180 + 3) \\times (370 + 3)\n\\]\n\nExpanding this, we get:\n\n\\[\n180 \\times 370 + 180 \\times 3 + 3 \\times 370 + 3 \\times 3\n\\]\n\nCalculating each term separately:\n\n1. \\( 180 \\times 370 \\):\n   \\[\n   180 \\times 370 = 66,600\n   \\]\n\n2. \\( 180 \\times 3 \\):\n   \\[\n   180 \\times 3 = 540\n   \\]\n\n3. \\( 3 \\times 370 \\):\n   \\[\n   3 \\times 370 = 1,110\n   \\]\n\n4. \\( 3 \\times 3 \\):\n   \\[\n   3 \\times 3 = 9\n   \\]\n\nAdding all these results together:\n\n\\[\n66,600 + 540 + 1,110 + 9 = 68,259\n\\]\n\nTo verify, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. Multiply 183 by 3 (units digit of 373):\n   \\[\n   3 \\times 183 = 549\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 183 by 7 (tens digit of 373):\n   \\[\n   7 \\times 183 = 1,281 \\quad \\text{(with a carryover of 1)}\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 183 by 3 (hundreds digit of 373):\n   \\[\n   3 \\times 183 = 549 \\quad \\text{(with a carryover of 1)}\n   \\]\n\nCombining the partial products:\n\n\\[\n549 \\quad 1286 \\quad 550\n\\]\n\nAdding these together:\n\n\\[\n549 + 1286 + 550 = 68,259\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 183 and 373 is \\(\\boxed{68259}\\).",
