s the same result as before. So 268,223. So that seems correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use another method. Let's see. 361 is 360 + 1. So 360 \u00d7 743 + 1 \u00d7 743.\n\n360 \u00d7 743. Let's compute that.\n\n360 \u00d7 700 = 252,000.\n\n360 \u00d7 40 = 14,400.\n\n360 \u00d7 3 = 1,080.\n\nAdding those: 252,000 + 14,400 = 266,400. Then +1,080 = 267,480.\n\nThen add 743: 267,480 + 743 = 268,223. Again, same result. So that's three different methods giving me 268,223. That gives me confidence that the answer is correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use a calculator to check. But since I don't have a calculator here, but let me verify with another approach.\n\nAnother way: 361 \u00d7 743. Let's note that 361 is 19 squared, but I don't know if that helps here. Alternatively, 743 is a prime? Not sure. Maybe not helpful.\n\nAlternatively, use the fact that 361 \u00d7 743 = (360 + 1)(700 + 40 + 3). Wait, that's similar to the first method. But we already did that.\n\nAlternatively, use the difference of squares? Hmm, 743 - 360 = 383. Not sure. Maybe not helpful.\n\nAlternatively, approximate. 361 is about 360, 743 is about 700. 360 \u00d7 700 = 252,000. Then, 360 \u00d7 43 = 15,480. So 252,000 + 15,480 = 267,480. Then add 1 \u00d7 743 = 743. 267,480 + 743 = 268,223. Yep, same answer.\n\nSo all methods lead to 268,223. Therefore, I think that's the correct product.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 361 and 743 is \\boxed{268223}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 361 and 743, we can use the distributive property:\n\n\\[\n361 \\times 743 = (300 + 60 + 1) \\times (700 + 40 + 3)\n\\]\n\nExpanding this using the distributive property:\n\n\\[\n= 300 \\times 700 + 300 \\times 40 + 300 \\times 3 + 60 \\times 700 + 60 \\times 40 + 60 \\times 3 + 1 \\times 700 + 1 \\times 40 + 1 \\times 3\n\\]\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n\\[\n300 \\times 700 = 210000\n\\]\n\\[\n300 \\times 40 = 12000\n\\]\n\\[\n300 \\times 3 = 900\n\\]\n\\[\n60 \\times 700 = 42000\n\\]\n\\[\n60 \\times 40 = 2400\n\