0 + 60 + 1\\) and 526 into \\(500 + 20 + 6\\).\n   - Multiply each term and sum the results:\n     \\[\n     \\begin{align*}\n     (700 \\times 500) + (700 \\times 20) + (700 \\times 6) & = 350,000 + 14,000 + 4,200 \\\\\n     (60 \\times 500) + (60 \\times 20) + (60 \\times 6) & = 30,000 + 1,200 + 360 \\\\\n     (1 \\times 500) + (1 \\times 20) + (1 \\times 6) & = 500 + 20 + 6 \\\\\n     \\end{align*}\n     \\]\n   - Adding all these results together:\n     \\[\n     350,000 + 14,000 + 4,200 + 30,000 + 1,200 + 360 + 500 + 20 + 6 = 399,286\n     \\]\n\n2. **Using the standard multiplication method:**\n   - Multiply 761 by 6, 20, and 500, then shift appropriately and sum the results:\n     \\[\n     \\begin{align*}\n     761 \\times 6 & = 4,566 \\\\\n     761 \\times 20 & = 15,220 \\quad \\text{(shifted one position)} \\\\\n     761 \\times 500 & = 380,500 \\quad \\text{(shifted two positions)} \\\\\n     \\end{align*}\n     \\]\n   - Adding the partial products:\n     \\[\n     4,566 + 15,220 + 380,500 = 399,286\n     \\]\n\n3. **Verification using alternative methods:**\n   - Breaking down 526 into 500 + 26 and using distributive property again confirms the result.\n   - Summing the partial products from different methods consistently results in 399,286.\n\nThus, the product of 761 and 526 is \\(\\boxed{399286}\\).",
