489,244\n\nYes, because 65,044 + 424,200. 65,044 + 400,000 = 465,044. Then add 24,200: 465,044 + 24,200 = 489,244. That seems right.\n\nSo the total product is 489,244. Let me check if that makes sense. Let me do a quick check by adding the two numbers in another way or using estimation.\n\n707 is close to 700, and 692 is close to 700. So 700 \u00d7 700 = 490,000. But since both numbers are slightly less than 700, the actual product should be a bit less than 490,000. Our answer is 489,244, which is indeed 766 less than 490,000. That seems reasonable.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use the distributive property to break it down. Let's see:\n\n707 \u00d7 692 = (700 + 7) \u00d7 (700 - 8) [since 692 = 700 - 8]\n\nUsing the formula (a + b)(a - b) = a\u00b2 - b\u00b2, but here it's (700 + 7)(700 - 8). Wait, that's not the difference of squares. Hmm. Maybe it's better to just expand it normally.\n\nSo, (700 + 7)(700 - 8) = 700\u00d7700 + 700\u00d7(-8) + 7\u00d7700 + 7\u00d7(-8)\n\nCalculate each term:\n\n700\u00d7700 = 490,000\n\n700\u00d7(-8) = -5,600\n\n7\u00d7700 = 4,900\n\n7\u00d7(-8) = -56\n\nNow, add them all together:\n\n490,000 - 5,600 + 4,900 - 56\n\nFirst, 490,000 - 5,600 = 484,400\n\nThen, 484,400 + 4,900 = 489,300\n\nThen, 489,300 - 56 = 489,244\n\nOh, that's the same result as before! So that confirms it. So using the distributive property also gives 489,244. That's reassuring.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can check using a calculator. But since I don't have a calculator here, maybe another estimation. Let's see:\n\n707 \u00d7 692. Let's approximate 707 as 700 and 692 as 700. Then 700 \u00d7 700 = 490,000. But since 707 is 7 more than 700 and 692 is 8 less than 700, the actual product is 700\u00d7700 + (7\u00d7700 - 700\u00d78) + 7\u00d7(-8). Wait, that's similar to the previous method. Which gives 490,000 + (4,900 - 5,600) - 56 = 490,000 - 700 - 56 = 490,000 - 756 = 489,244. Yep, same answer.\n\nSo both methods give the same result, so I feel confident that 489,244 is the correct product.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can check by multiplying 707 by 700 and then subtracting 707 times 8. Let's see:\n\n707 \u00d7 700 = 494,900\n\n707 \u00d7 8 = 5,656\n\nSo, 494,900 - 5,656 = 489,244. Exactly the same. So that's another way to confirm.\n\nTherefore, regardless of the method I use, the product is 489,244. So I think that's the answer.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 707 and 692 is \\boxed{489244}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 707 and 692, we can use the standard multiplication method:\n\n1. Multiply 707 by the rightmost digit of 692 (2):\n   \\[\n   707 \\times 2 = 1414\n   \\]\n   Write down 1414 and shift it one position to the left.\n\n2. Multiply 707 by the middle digit of 692 (9):\n   \\[\n   707 \\times 9 = 6363\n   \\]\n   Write down 6363 and shift it one position to the left.\n\n3. Multiply 707 by the leftmost digit of 692 (6):\n   \\[\n   707 \\times 6 = 4242\n   \\]\n   Write down 4242 and shift it two positions to the left.\n\n4. Add the partial products together:\n   \\[\n   1414 + 63630 + 424200 = 489244\n   \\]\n\nWe can also verify this using the distributive property:\n   \\[\n   (700 + 7)(700 - 8) = 700 \\times 700 + 700 \\times (-8) + 7 \\times 700 + 7 \\times (-8)\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   = 490000 - 5600 + 4900 - 56 = 490000 - 756 = 489244\n   \\]\n\nThus, the product of 707 and 692 is \\(\\boxed{489244}\\).",
