es (200 + 26)\n\\]\n\nFirst, calculate \\(100 \\times 200\\):\n\n\\[\n100 \\times 200 = 20000\n\\]\n\nNext, calculate \\(100 \\times 26\\):\n\n\\[\n100 \\times 26 = 2600\n\\]\n\nAdd these two results together:\n\n\\[\n20000 + 2600 = 22600\n\\]\n\nAnother way to verify this is by recognizing that multiplying by 100 adds two zeros to the end of the number. Therefore, multiplying 226 by 100:\n\n\\[\n226 \\times 100 = 22600\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 100 and 226 is \\(\\boxed{22600}\\).",
