1460 + 31. 271460 + 30 is 271490, then +1 is 271491. Yes, that seems right.\n\nSo, putting it all together, the product of 433 and 726 is 271,491. Let me verify this with another method to make sure I didn't make a mistake. Maybe using the distributive property?\n\nAlternatively, I can think of 726 as 700 + 26. So, 433*700 + 433*26. Let's compute each part.\n\nFirst, 433*700. 433*7 = 3031, so 433*700 = 3031*10 = 30,310.\n\nNext, 433*26. Let's break that down into 433*20 + 433*6. 433*20 = 8,660. 433*6 = 2,598. Adding those together: 8,660 + 2,598. Let's compute 8,660 + 2,000 = 10,660, then +598 = 11,258.\n\nNow, add 30,310 + 11,258. Let's do that. 30,310 + 10,000 = 40,310, then +1,258. 40,310 + 1,000 = 41,310, then +258 = 41,568. Wait, that's different from the previous result. Hmm, that's a problem. So, according to this method, the product is 41,568, but according to the standard multiplication, it's 271,491. There's a discrepancy here. That means I made a mistake somewhere.\n\nLet me check the second method again. First, 433*700. 433*7 is 3031, so 3031*10 is 30,310. That seems correct. Then 433*26. Let's compute 433*20 and 433*6 again. 433*20: 433*2=866, so 866*10=8,660. Correct. 433*6=2,598. Correct. Then 8,660 + 2,598. Let's add 8,660 + 2,000 = 10,660. Then 10,660 + 598. 10,660 + 500 = 11,160. Then +98 = 11,258. So that's correct. Then 30,310 + 11,258. Let's add 30,310 + 10,000 = 40,310. Then 40,310 + 1,258. 40,310 + 1,000 = 41,310. Then 41,310 + 258. 41,310 + 200 = 41,510. Then +58 = 41,568. Hmm, so according to this, the product is 41,568. But the standard multiplication gave me 271,491. These two results are different. That means I messed up somewhere in the first method.\n\nWait, so where did I go wrong? Let's go back to the standard multiplication step by step.\n\nOriginal problem: 433 * 726.\n\nFirst, multiply 433 by 6 (units place of 726):\n\n433*6. Let's compute again. 400*6=2400, 30*6=180, 3*6=18. 2400+180=2580, 2580+18=2598. That's correct.\n\nThen, shift left by one (multiply by 10) and add 433*2 (tens place of 726):\n\n2598 (from 433*6) shifted left becomes 25980. Then 433*2=866. Adding 25980 + 866. Let's do this again. 25980 + 800 = 26780. Then 26780 + 66 = 26846. Correct.\n\nThen, shift left again (multiply by 10) and add 433*7 (hundreds place of 726):\n\n26846 shifted left becomes 268460. Then 433*7=3031. Adding 268460 + 3031. Let's check this again. 268,460 + 3,000 = 271,460. Then 271,460 + 31 = 271,491. Wait, but in the second method, I got 41,568. That's way off. So, there's a mistake here. But where?\n\nWait, hold on. The second method was breaking 726 into 700 + 26. So, 433*700 + 433*26. But 433*700 is 30,310 and 433*26 is 11,258. Then 30,310 + 11,258 is 41,568. But according to the standard multiplication, it's 271,491. These numbers are completely different. That means one of the methods is wrong. But which one?\n\nWait, maybe I messed up the second method. Let me check 433*26 again. 433*26. Let's compute 433*20 + 433*6. 433*20: 433*2=866, so 866*10=8,660. Correct. 433*6=2,598. Correct. Then 8,660 + 2,598. Let's compute 8,660 + 2,598. 8,660 + 2,000 = 10,660. 10,660 + 598. 10,660 + 500 = 11,160. 11,160 + 98 = 11,258. Correct. Then 30,310 + 11,258. 30,310 + 10,000 = 40,310. 40,310 + 1,258. 40,310 + 1,000 = 41,310. 41,310 + 258. 41,310 + 200 = 41,510. 41,510 + 58 = 41,568. So that's correct. But according to standard multiplication, it's 271,491. So, which one is correct?\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the standard multiplication. Let me check that again.\n\nOriginal problem: 433 * 726.\n\nStep 1: Multiply 433 by 6 (units digit of 726):\n\n433*6. Let's compute again. 400*6=2400, 30*6=180, 3*6=18. 2400+180=2580, 2580+18=2598. Correct.\n\nStep 2: Multiply 433 by 2 (tens digit of 726), shift left (multiply by 10):\n\n2598*10=25,980. Then 433*2=866. 25,980 + 866. Let's compute 25,980 + 800=26,780. Then 26,780 + 66=26,846. Correct.\n\nStep 3: Multiply 433 by 7 (hundreds digit of 726), shift left again (mu