ck. But since I don't have a calculator here, let me try another way.\n\nAlternatively, 704 x 939. Let's compute 704 x 900 = 633,600. Then 704 x 30 = 21,120. Then 704 x 9 = 6,336. Adding those gives 633,600 + 21,120 = 654,720; 654,720 + 6,336 = 661,056. Yep, same answer.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the standard algorithm step by step again to confirm.\n\nLet me write it out again:\n\n      704\n    x 939\n    -------\n\nFirst, multiply 704 by 9:\n\n704\nx   9\n-----\n6336\n\nThen, multiply 704 by 3 (next digit, shifted one position):\n\n   704\n  x  3\n-----\n2112\n   0\n-----\n21120\n\nThen, multiply 704 by 9 (next digit, shifted two positions):\n\n   704\n  x  9\n-----\n6336\n   0\n   0\n-----\n633600\n\nNow, adding them up:\n\n633600\n+ 21120\n+   6336\n= 661,056\n\nYes, that's the same as before. So I think that's correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe check with another multiplication method. For example, breaking down 939 into 900 + 30 + 9, which we already did, and that worked.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the fact that 704 x 939 = 704 x (900 + 30 + 9) = 704*900 + 704*30 + 704*9. Which we did, and got 633,600 + 21,120 + 6,336 = 661,056.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the standard multiplication algorithm step by step:\n\nMultiply 704 by 9:\n\n704\nx   9\n-----\n6336\n\nMultiply 704 by 3 (tens place):\n\n704\n  x 3\n-----\n2112\n\nMultiply 704 by 9 (hundreds place):\n\n704\n  x 9\n-----\n6336\n\nThen, writing them down:\n\n6336\n 2112\n 6336\n-------\n661056\n\nWait, but when adding, the alignment is important. Let me make sure:\n\nThe first partial product is 6336 (four digits).\n\nThe second partial product is 2112 shifted one position to the left, so it's 21120 (five digits).\n\nThe third partial product is 6336 shifted two positions to the left, so it's 633600 (six digits).\n\nSo when adding:\n\n633600 (6 digits)\n+ 21120 (5 digits)\n+   6336 (4 digits)\n= 661056 (6 digits)\n\nYes, that's correct. So the total is 661,056.\n\nTherefore, I think the answer is 661,056.