e hundreds place, shifted two positions to the left)\n   ------\n   Now add them up:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n1,770\n\n+  8850 (shifted one position left)\n\n+  8,850 (shifted two positions left)\n\nWait, let me write them aligned properly:\n\n      1,770\n\n    + 8,850\n\n    +88,500\n\nAdding these together:\n\nFirst, 1,770 + 8,850. Let's do 1,770 + 8,850. 1,770 + 8,000 = 9,770. Then +850 = 10,620.\n\nThen add 88,500 to 10,620. 10,620 + 88,500. 10,000 + 88,500 = 98,500. Then +620 = 99,120.\n\nWait, that's different from the previous result. Hmm, so now I get 99,120. But earlier I got 90,270. There must be a mistake here.\n\nWait, maybe I messed up the alignment. Let me try again.\n\nIn standard multiplication:\n\n     885\n\n   x 102\n\n   ------\n     885 * 2 = 1,770 (this is the 2 in the ones place, so it's 1,770)\n\n     885 * 0 = 0 (this is the 0 in the tens place, so it's 0, but shifted one position to the left, so 8,850)\n\n     885 * 1 = 885 (this is the 1 in the hundreds place, shifted two positions to the left, so 88,500)\n\nNow, adding these three numbers:\n\n1,770\n\n+ 8,850\n\n+88,500\n\nLet's add 1,770 and 8,850 first. 1,770 + 8,850. Let's break it down:\n\n1,000 + 8,000 = 9,000\n\n700 + 800 = 1,500\n\n70 + 50 = 120\n\nSo total is 9,000 + 1,500 = 10,500 + 120 = 10,620.\n\nThen add 88,500 to 10,620. 88,500 + 10,000 = 98,500. Then 98,500 + 620 = 99,120.\n\nBut earlier, when I did the distributive method, I got 90,270. These two results are different. That means I made a mistake somewhere. Let me check both methods again.\n\nFirst method: breaking down 885 into 800 + 80 + 5 and 102 into 100 + 2.\n\nCalculations:\n\n800*100 = 80,000\n\n800*2 = 1,600\n\n80*100 = 8,000\n\n80*2 = 160\n\n5*100 = 500\n\n5*2 = 10\n\nAdding them up: 80,000 + 1,600 = 81,600; 81,600 + 8,000 = 89,600; 89,600 + 160 = 89,760; 89,760 + 500 = 90,260; 90,260 + 10 = 90,270.\n\nSecond method: standard multiplication gives 99,120.\n\nHmm, so which one is correct? Let me verify with another method. Maybe using another approach.\n\nAlternatively, 102 is 100 + 2, so 885*102 = 885*(100 + 2) = 885*100 + 885*2 = 88,500 + 1,770 = 90,270. Wait, that's the same as the first method. So why does the standard multiplication give 99,120?\n\nWait, maybe I messed up the standard multiplication steps. Let me try again.\n\nStandard multiplication:\n\n     885\n\n   x 102\n\n   ------\n     885 * 2 = 1,770 (this is correct for the 2 in the ones place)\n\n     885 * 0 = 0 (but shifted one place to the left, so it's 8,850)\n\n     885 * 1 = 885 (shifted two places to the left, so it's 88,500)\n\nNow, adding:\n\n1,770\n\n+ 8,850\n\n+88,500\n\nLet me add 1,770 and 8,850 first. 1,770 + 8,850. Let's do 1,000 + 8,000 = 9,000. Then 700 + 800 = 1,500. Then 70 + 50 = 120. So total is 9,000 + 1,500 = 10,500 + 120 = 10,620. Then add 88,500. 10,620 + 88,500. 10,000 + 88,500 = 98,500. Then 620 + 0 = 620. So 98,500 + 620 = 99,120.\n\nWait, but according to the distributive method, it's 90,270. So which is correct?\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the standard multiplication. Let me check 885*100. 885*100 is 88,500. Correct. Then 885*2 is 1,770. Correct. Then adding 88,500 + 1,770. 88,500 + 1,000 = 89,500. Then +770 = 90,270. Oh! Wait, here's the mistake. When adding 88,500 + 1,770, I should get 90,270. But earlier, I added 88,500 + 8,850 first, which was wrong.\n\nWait, no. Wait, in the standard multiplication, the three numbers to add are 1,770 (from 885*2), 8,850 (from 885*0 shifted left by one), and 88,500 (from 885*1 shifted left by two). So adding them:\n\n1,770 + 8,850 + 88,500.\n\nBut if I add 1,770 + 8,850 first, that's 10,620. Then 10,620 + 88,500 = 99,120. But according to distributive method, it's 90,270. So which is correct?\n\nWait, maybe I messed up the standard multiplication steps. Let me check 885*102.\n\nAlternatively, let's compute 885*102 using another method. Let's compute 885*100 = 88,500. Then 885*2 = 1,770. Then 88,500 + 1,770 = 90,270. That's correct