r here, but I can estimate. 210 is approximately 200, and 897 is approximately 900. So 200\u00d7900=180,000. The actual answer is 188,370, which is 8,370 more than 180,000. That seems reasonable. \n\nAlternatively, 210 is 200 + 10, so 200\u00d7897=179,400 and 10\u00d7897=8,970. Adding them gives 188,370. Yep, that's consistent. \n\nI think I've verified it enough ways. The answer must be 188,370.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 210 and 897 is \\boxed{188370}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 210 and 897, we can use the distributive property:\n\n\\[\n210 \\times 897 = (200 + 10) \\times 897 = 200 \\times 897 + 10 \\times 897\n\\]\n\nFirst, calculate \\(200 \\times 897\\):\n\n\\[\n200 \\times 897 = 2 \\times 897 \\times 100 = 1794 \\times 100 = 179400\n\\]\n\nNext, calculate \\(10 \\times 897\\):\n\n\\[\n10 \\times 897 = 8970\n\\]\n\nAdd the results together:\n\n\\[\n179400 + 8970 = 188370\n\\]\n\nWe can also verify this using another method by recognizing that \\(897 = 900 - 3\\):\n\n\\[\n210 \\times 897 = 210 \\times (900 - 3) = 210 \\times 900 - 210 \\times 3\n\\]\n\nCalculate \\(210 \\times 900\\):\n\n\\[\n210 \\times 900 = 189000\n\\]\n\nSubtract \\(210 \\times 3\\):\n\n\\[\n210 \\times 3 = 630\n\\]\n\n\\[\n189000 - 630 = 188370\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 210 and 897 is \\(\\boxed{188370}\\).",
