pt adding 10,000 each time, which led me to over 1,000,000. But breaking it down into smaller parts shows that the correct total is 243,660. \n\nTherefore, the product of 465 and 524 is 243,660. Let me verify this with another method to be sure. \n\nAnother way to multiply 465 by 524 is to use the fact that 524 is 500 + 24. So, 465*500 + 465*24. \n\nFirst, 465*500. 465*5=2325, so 465*500=232,500. \n\nThen, 465*24. Let's compute that. 465*20=9,300 and 465*4=1,860. So 9,300 + 1,860 = 11,160. \n\nAdding 232,500 + 11,160 = 243,660. Yep, same result. So that confirms it. \n\nAlternatively, maybe using the standard algorithm again but being more careful. \n\nMultiplying 465 by 524:\n\nFirst, write 465\nx 524\n--------\nStart with the ones digit: 4\n465\nx   4\n-----\n1860  (which is 465*4)\n\nNext, the tens digit: 2\nBut since it's the tens place, we shift one position to the left:\n465\nx  2\n-----\n9300  (465*2, shifted left by one)\n\nNext, the hundreds digit: 5\nShifted two positions to the left:\n465\nx  5\n-----\n232500  (465*5, shifted left by two)\n\nNow, add them up:\n\n1860\n+9300\n------\n11,160\n\n11,160\n+232,500\n---------\n243,660\n\nYes, that's the same as before. So, the product is 243,660. \n\nJust to make sure, let me check with a calculator. Well, since I don't have a calculator here, but I can cross-verify with another multiplication method. \n\nAlternatively, 465 * 524. Let's compute 465*500 = 232,500 and 465*24 = 11,160. Then, 232,500 + 11,160. 232,500 + 10,000 = 242,500; 242,500 + 1,160 = 243,660. Yep, same result. \n\nTherefore, I'm confident that the product of 465 and 524 is 243,660.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 465 and 524 is \\boxed{243660}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 465 and 524, we can break down the multiplication into simpler steps using the distributive property.\n\nFirst, we split 524 into 500 + 20 + 4 and multiply each part by 465:\n\n1. Multiply 465 by 4:\n   \\[\n   465 \\times 4 = 1860\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 465 by 20 (which is 2 \\times 10) and shift the result one position to the left:\n   \\[\n   465 \\times 2 = 930 \\quad \\text{then} \\quad 930 \\times 10 = 9300\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 465 by 500 (which is 5 \\times 100) and shift the result two positions to the left:\n   \\[\n   465 \\times 5 = 2325 \\quad \\text{then} \\quad 2325 \\times 100 = 232500\n   \\]\n\nNext, we add the partial products together:\n\\[\n1860 + 9300 + 232500\n\\]\n\n1. Add 1860 and 9300:\n   \\[\n   1860 + 9300 = 11160\n   \\]\n\n2. Add the result to 232500:\n   \\[\n   11160 + 232500 = 243660\n   \\]\n\nThus, the product of 465 and 524 is \\(\\boxed{243660}\\).",
