2\n+91200\n=?\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n2 + 0 = 2\n\n7 + 0 = 7\n\n1 + 0 = 1\n\n1 + 2 = 3\n\n1 + 1 = 2\n\nSo that's 102,372. Wait, that seems correct. Let me verify with another method.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use the distributive property. Let's see. 228 x 449 can be written as 228 x (400 + 40 + 9). Which is the same as 228x400 + 228x40 + 228x9, which is exactly what I did before. So that gives me 91200 + 9120 + 2052. Which adds up to 102,372. Hmm, okay.\n\nBut let me check with another approach to make sure. Maybe breaking down 449 into 450 - 1. So 228 x 449 = 228 x (450 - 1) = 228x450 - 228x1. Let's compute that.\n\n228 x 450. Well, 228 x 400 = 91,200. 228 x 50 = 11,400. So 91,200 + 11,400 = 102,600. Then subtract 228: 102,600 - 228 = 102,372. So that's the same result. Okay, so that's a good confirmation.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using another multiplication method. Let's try multiplying 228 by 449 using the standard multiplication algorithm step by step.\n\nFirst, write 228\n    x 449\nThen, multiply 228 by 9:\n    2052\nMultiply 228 by 40 (shift one position to the left):\n    9120\nMultiply 228 by 400 (shift two positions to the left):\n    91200\nNow, add them up:\n    2052\n+ 9120\n+ 91200\n= 102,372\n\nYes, that's the same as before. So seems like 102,372 is the correct product.\n\nWait, but let me check with a calculator to be absolutely sure. Since I don't have a calculator here, maybe I can compute 228 x 449 another way.\n\nAlternatively, maybe breaking down 228 into 200 + 28. So 200 x 449 = 89,800. Then 28 x 449. Let's compute 28 x 400 = 11,200. 28 x 40 = 1,120. 28 x 9 = 252. So adding those: 11,200 + 1,120 = 12,320. Then 12,320 + 252 = 12,572. Then total is 89,800 + 12,572 = 102,372. Yep, same answer. So that's another confirmation.\n\nOkay, so all methods lead to 102,372. Therefore, the product of 228 and 449 is 102,372.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 228 and 449 is \\boxed{102372}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 228 and 449, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. Multiply 228 by the ones digit (9) of 449:\n   \\[\n   228 \\times 9 = 2052\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 228 by the tens digit (4) of 449, then add a zero:\n   \\[\n   228 \\times 4 = 912 \\quad \\text{so} \\quad 9120\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 228 by the hundreds digit (4) of 449, then add two zeros:\n   \\[\n   228 \\times 4 = 912 \\quad \\text{so} \\quad 91200\n   \\]\n\n4. Add the results of the three multiplications:\n   \\[\n   2052 + 9120 + 91200 = 102372\n   \\]\n\nWe can also verify this using the distributive property:\n   \\[\n   228 \\times 449 = 228 \\times (450 - 1) = 228 \\times 450 - 228 \\times 1\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   228 \\times 450 = 91200 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 228 \\times 1 = 228\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   91200 - 228 = 102372\n   \\]\n\nThus, the product of 228 and 449 is \\(\\boxed{102372}\\).",
