f squares or some other identity, but since these numbers aren't close to squares, that might not help. \n\nAlternatively, break down 843 into 800 + 40 + 3, which we already did. \n\nAlternatively, use the fact that 843 = 800 + 43. Then, 402*800 + 402*43. Let's see:\n\n402*800 = 321,600\n\n402*43: Let's compute that. 402*40=16,080 and 402*3=1,206. So 16,080 + 1,206 = 17,286. \n\nThen, 321,600 + 17,286 = 338,886. \n\nSame result again. \n\nSo, all methods lead to 338,886. Therefore, I can be confident that the product of 402 and 843 is 338,886. \n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 402 and 843 is \\boxed{338886}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 402 and 843, we can break down 402 into 400 + 2 and multiply each part by 843, then add the results together.\n\nFirst, compute \\(400 \\times 843\\):\n\\[\n400 \\times 843 = 4 \\times 843 \\times 100 = 3372 \\times 100 = 337200\n\\]\n\nNext, compute \\(2 \\times 843\\):\n\\[\n2 \\times 843 = 1686\n\\]\n\nAdd the two results together:\n\\[\n337200 + 1686 = 338886\n\\]\n\nWe can verify this using the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n402 \\times 843 \\\\\n\\hline\n1206 \\quad \\text{(402 \\times 3)} \\\\\n16080 \\quad \\text{(402 \\times 40)} \\\\\n321600 \\quad \\text{(402 \\times 800)} \\\\\n\\hline\n338886 \\quad \\text{(sum of the results)}\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 402 and 843 is \\(\\boxed{338886}\\).",
