duct is 2838.\n\nAlternatively, maybe there's a different way to compute this to cross-verify. Let's see. 473 x 402. Hmm, 473 is 400 + 70 + 3, and 402 is 400 + 0 + 2. So, expanding the multiplication:\n\n(400 + 70 + 3) x (400 + 0 + 2) = 400x400 + 400x0 + 400x2 + 70x400 + 70x0 + 70x2 + 3x400 + 3x0 + 3x2.\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n400x400 = 160,000\n\n400x0 = 0\n\n400x2 = 800\n\n70x400 = 28,000\n\n70x0 = 0\n\n70x2 = 140\n\n3x400 = 1,200\n\n3x0 = 0\n\n3x2 = 6\n\nNow, adding all these together:\n\n160,000 + 0 + 800 + 28,000 + 0 + 140 + 1,200 + 0 + 6.\n\nLet's add them step by step:\n\n160,000 + 800 = 160,800\n\n160,800 + 28,000 = 188,800\n\n188,800 + 140 = 188,940\n\n188,940 + 1,200 = 189,140\n\n189,140 + 6 = 189,146\n\nWait, hold on, that's different from the previous result. Wait, this can't be. There must be a mistake here. Let me check again.\n\nWait, no. Wait, in the first method, I had 946 + 0 + 1892 = 2838. But in the second method, expanding, I get 160,000 + 800 + 28,000 + 140 + 1,200 + 6. Let me compute that again:\n\n160,000 + 800 = 160,800\n\n160,800 + 28,000 = 188,800\n\n188,800 + 140 = 188,940\n\n188,940 + 1,200 = 189,140\n\n189,140 + 6 = 189,146\n\nWait, but 189,146 is way larger than 2838. That can't be. So, clearly, I made a mistake in one of the methods. Let me check where.\n\nWait, in the first method, when I broke down 402 into 400, 0, and 2, then multiplied each by 473 and added. So, 473 x 400 is 189,200. Then 473 x 0 is 0. Then 473 x 2 is 946. Then adding 189,200 + 0 + 946 = 189,200 + 946 = 190,146. Wait, hold on, that's different from the first calculation. Wait, so now I'm confused.\n\nWait, maybe I messed up the first method. Let me go back.\n\nOriginal first method:\n\nFirst, multiply 473 by the units digit (2): 473 x 2 = 946.\n\nThen, multiply 473 by the tens digit (0): 473 x 0 = 0.\n\nThen, multiply 473 by the hundreds digit (4): 473 x 4 = 1,892.\n\nThen, add them up: 946 + 0 + 1,892.\n\nWait, 946 + 1,892. Let's compute that. 946 + 1,892. 9