4,150 + 1,314. Let's split 1,314 into 1,000 + 300 + 14.\n\n624,150 + 1,000 = 625,150\n\n625,150 + 300 = 625,450\n\n625,450 + 14 = 625,464. Okay, that seems correct.\n\nSo the total is 625,464. Let me verify this with another method to make sure I didn't make a mistake.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use the standard multiplication algorithm to cross-check.\n\nMultiplying 657 by 952:\n\nFirst, write 657 \u00d7 952. Let's do it step by step.\n\nMultiply 657 by 2: 1,314\n\nMultiply 657 by 50: 32,850\n\nMultiply 657 by 900: 591,300\n\nAdd them up: 1,314 + 32,850 = 34,164; 34,164 + 591,300 = 625,464. Yep, same result. So that seems to check out.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use another decomposition. Let's see, 952 is 900 + 50 + 2, which we already did. Alternatively, 952 is 950 + 2. Let's try that.\n\n657 \u00d7 952 = 657 \u00d7 (950 + 2) = 657\u00d7950 + 657\u00d72\n\nCompute 657\u00d7950. Hmm, 657\u00d7950 is 657\u00d7(900 + 50) = 657\u00d7900 + 657\u00d750 = 591,300 + 32,850 = 624,150. Then add 657\u00d72 = 1,314. So 624,150 + 1,314 = 625,464. Same result. So that's consistent.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the distributive property in another way. Let's see:\n\n657 \u00d7 952. Let's write 952 as (1000 - 48). So 657 \u00d7 952 = 657 \u00d7 1000 - 657 \u00d7 48.\n\nCompute 657 \u00d7 1000 = 657,000\n\nCompute 657 \u00d7 48. Let's break that down: 657 \u00d7 40 + 657 \u00d7 8.\n\n657 \u00d7 40: 600 \u00d7 40 = 24,000; 57 \u00d7 40 = 2,280. So 24,000 + 2,280 = 26,280.\n\n657 \u00d7 8: 600 \u00d7 8 = 4,800; 57 \u00d7 8 = 456. So 4,800 + 456 = 5,256.\n\nSo 657 \u00d7 48 = 26,280 + 5,256 = 31,536.\n\nTherefore, 657 \u00d7 952 = 657,000 - 31,536 = 625,464. Again, same answer. So that's three different methods giving me 625,464. That gives me confidence that the answer is correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use a calculator to check, but since I don't have one here, I need to rely on my mental math. Let me try another approach. Let's use the fact that 657 \u00d7 952 is equal to (600 + 57) \u00d7 952.\n\nCompute 600 \u00d7 952 = 571,200 (since 600\u00d7900=540,000; 600\u00d752=31,200; 540,000 +31,200=571,200)\n\nCompute 57 \u00d7 952. Let's do that. 50 \u00d7 952 = 47,600; 7 \u00d7 952 = 6,664. So 47,600 + 6,664 = 54,264.\n\nThen add 571,200 + 54,264. 571,200 + 50,000 = 621,200; 621,200 + 4,264 = 625,464. Again, same result. So that's four different methods, all leading to 625,464. I think that's solid.\n\nTherefore, the product of 657 and 952 is 625,464.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 657 and 952 is \\boxed{625464}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 657 and 952, we can break down 952 into 900 + 50 + 2 and multiply each component separately:\n\n\\[\n657 \\times 952 = 657 \\times (900 + 50 + 2) = 657 \\times 900 + 657 \\times 50 + 657 \\times 2\n\\]\n\n1. Calculate \\(657 \\times 900\\):\n   \\[\n   657 \\times 900 = 657 \\times 9 \\times 100 = 5913 \\times 100 = 591300\n   \\]\n\n2. Calculate \\(657 \\times 50\\):\n   \\[\n   657 \\times 50 = 657 \\times 5 \\times 10 = 3285 \\times 10 = 32850\n   \\]\n\n3. Calculate \\(657 \\times 2\\):\n   \\[\n   657 \\times 2 = 1314\n   \\]\n\n4. Add the results together:\n   \\[\n   591300 + 32850 + 1314\n   \\]\n\n   First, add \\(591300\\) and \\(32850\\):\n   \\[\n   591300 + 32850 = 624150\n   \\]\n\n   Then, add \\(1314\\) to the result:\n   \\[\n   624150 + 1314 = 625464\n   \\]\n\nThus, the product of 657 and 952 is \\(\\boxed{625464}\\).",
