 that might be more complicated. Let me try.\n\n9.3 * 6.76. Let's convert them to whole numbers by multiplying by 1000: 9300 * 6760 / 10000. But that seems more involved. Maybe not the best approach.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the fact that 676 is 600 + 76, which we already did. Wait, but we already confirmed that two different methods give 628,680. So maybe that's the correct answer.\n\nBut just to be thorough, let me try another way. Let's use the standard multiplication algorithm step by step.\n\nMultiplying 930 by 676:\n\nFirst, write 930\n        x 676\n        ------\nStart with the units digit of 676, which is 6. Multiply 6 by 930. 6*930 = 5,580. Write that under the line.\n\n        5580\n        ------\nNext, the tens digit of 676 is 7. Multiply 7 by 930. 7*930 = 6,510. Write that next to the previous result, shifted one position to the left.\n\n        5580\n       6510\n       ------\nNext, the hundreds digit of 676 is 6. Multiply 6 by 930. 6*930 = 5,580. Write that shifted two positions to the left.\n\n        5580\n       6510\n      5580\n      ------\nNow, add them all up:\n\n5580\n6510\n5580\n------\nLet's add the units place: 0 + 0 + 0 = 0.\n\nTens place: 8 + 1 + 8 = 17. Write down 7, carry over 1.\n\nHundreds place: 5 + 5 + 5 = 15, plus the carried 1 is 16. Write down 6, carry over 1.\n\nThousands place: 5 + 6 + 5 = 16, plus the carried 1 is 17. Write down 7, carry over 1.\n\nTen-thousands place: 1, plus the carried 1 is 2.\n\nSo putting it all together: 628,680. Yep, same result. So that's three different methods giving the same answer. I think that's solid.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the calculator method, but since I don't have a calculator here, but given that all manual methods give the same result, I can be confident.\n\nWait, just to check, maybe do a quick check by estimation. 930 is approximately 900, and 676 is approximately 700. 900*700 is 630,000. The actual answer is 628,680, which is just 1,320 less than 630,000. That seems reasonable. So the answer is 628,680.\n\nI think that's correct. All methods converge to that number, so I'll go with that.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 930 and 676 is \\boxed{628680}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 930 and 676, we can use the distributive property:\n\n\\[\n930 \\times 676 = (900 + 30) \\times (600 + 76)\n\\]\n\nExpanding this, we get:\n\n\\[\n900 \\times 600 + 900 \\times 76 + 30 \\times 600 + 30 \\times 76\n\\]\n\nCalculating each term separately:\n\n1. \\(900 \\times 600 = 540,000\\)\n2. \\(900 \\times 76 = 68,400\\)\n3. \\(30 \\times 600 = 18,000\\)\n4. \\(30 \\times 76 = 2,280\\)\n\nAdding these results together:\n\n\\[\n540,000 + 68,400 + 18,000 + 2,280\n\\]\n\nFirst, add \\(540,000 + 68,400\\):\n\n\\[\n540,000 + 68,400 = 608,400\n\\]\n\nNext, add \\(18,000 + 2,280\\):\n\n\\[\n18,000 + 2,280 = 20,280\n\\]\n\nFinally, add the two results:\n\n\\[\n608,400 + 20,280 = 628,680\n\\]\n\nTo verify, we can use the standard multiplication method:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{r}\n930 & \\times & 676 \\\\\n & \\times & 676 \\\\\n\\hline\n5580 & \\quad (\\text{6} \\times 930) \\\\\n6510 & \\quad (\\text{7} \\times 930) \\\\\n5580 & \\quad (\\text{6} \\times 930) \\\\\n\\hline\n628680 & \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nAdding the results of each step confirms the product is 628,680.\n\nThus, the product of 930 and 676 is \\(\\boxed{628680}\\).",
