8. So that's 2883.\n\nBut again, this is shifted two places to the left because it's the hundreds digit. So that becomes 288300.\n\nNow, adding all three results together: 6573 (from 7) + 75120 (from 80) + 288300 (from 300).\n\nLet me add them step by step.\n\nFirst, 6573 + 75120. Let's see:\n\n6573 + 75120. Let's add 6000 + 75000 = 81000. Then 500 + 120 = 620. Then 70 + 3 = 73. Wait, maybe breaking it down:\n\n6573 + 75120:\n\n6573 + 75120 = (6000 + 500 + 70 + 3) + (70000 + 5000 + 120)\n\n= (6000 + 70000) + (500 + 5000) + (70 + 120) + 3\n\n= 76000 + 5500 + 190 + 3\n\n= 76000 + 5500 = 81500\n\n81500 + 190 = 81690\n\n81690 + 3 = 81693\n\nSo 6573 + 75120 = 81693\n\nNow add 288300 to that:\n\n81693 + 288300\n\nLet's break it down:\n\n80,000 + 280,000 = 360,000\n\n1,693 + 8,300 = 9,993\n\nSo 360,000 + 9,993 = 369,993\n\nWait, that seems high. Let me check again.\n\nWait, 81,693 + 288,300:\n\n81,693 + 200,000 = 281,693\n\n281,693 + 88,300 = 281,693 + 80,000 = 361,693; 361,693 + 8,300 = 369,993\n\nYes, that's correct. So the total is 369,993.\n\nWait, but let me verify this with another method to make sure.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using the distributive property. Let's see:\n\n939 x 387 can be written as (900 + 39) x (300 + 80 + 7)\n\nBut that might complicate. Alternatively, maybe breaking down 387 into 300 + 80 + 7 and multiplying each part by 939, then adding them up. Wait, that's similar to the standard multiplication method. So perhaps the result is 369,993.\n\nBut let me check with another approach. Let's use the calculator method in mind. 939 x 387.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using the fact that 939 is 900 + 39, and 387 is 300 + 80 + 7.\n\nSo:\n\n(900 + 39) x (300 + 80 + 7) = 900*(300 + 80 + 7) + 39*(300 + 80 + 7)\n\nCompute each part:\n\nFirst part: 900*300 = 270,000; 900*80 = 72,000; 900*7 = 6,300. So total 270,000 + 72,000 = 342,000; 342,000 + 6,300 = 348,300.\n\nSecond part: 39*300 = 11,700; 39*80 = 3,120; 39*7 = 273. So total 11,700 + 3,120 = 14,820; 14,820 + 273