00 is 281,700. Wait, hold on! Wait, here's the mistake. Earlier, I wrote 288300, but it's actually 281,700. Because 939*300 is 939*3*100, which is 2817*100=281,700. So in the first method, the third term should be 281,700, not 288,300. That was my mistake.\n\nSo correcting that:\n\nFirst method:\n\n6573 (from 7) + 75,120 (from 80) + 281,700 (from 300).\n\nAdding 6573 +75,120: 6573 +75,120. Let's compute:\n\n6573 +75,120. 6573 +70,000 =76,573; 76,573 +5,120 =81,693.\n\nThen add 281,700: 81,693 +281,700.\n\n81,693 +200,000 =281,693; 281,693 +81,700 =363,393.\n\nAh! So the first method actually also gives 363,393. So my initial calculation had a mistake in the third term, which was due to an incorrect multiplication. So both methods now agree on 363,393. Therefore, the correct product is 363,393.\n\nBut let me verify once more with another method. Let's use the standard algorithm again, but more carefully.\n\nMultiplying 939 by 387.\n\nLet me write it out:\n\n      939\n   x 387\n   -------\n\nFirst, multiply 939 by 7:\n\n7*9=63, carry 6.\n\n7*3=21 +6=27, carry 2.\n\n7*9=63 +2=65.\n\nSo that's 6573.\n\nNext, multiply 939 by 80 (the tens place, so shift one position left):\n\n8*9=72, carry 7.\n\n8*3=24 +7=31, carry 3.\n\n8*9=72 +3=75.\n\nSo that's 7512, then shifted left by one: 75120.\n\nNext, multiply 939 by 300 (the hundreds place, shift two positions left):\n\n3*9=27, carry 2.\n\n3*3=9 +2=11, carry 1.\n\n3*9=27 +1=28.\n\nSo that's 2883, then shifted left by two: 288300.\n\nNow, adding all three results:\n\n6573\n\n75120\n\n288300\n\nLet's add them step by step.\n\nFirst, 6573 +75120:\n\n6573 +75120. Let's add 6000 +75000=81000; 500 +120=620; 70 +0=70; 3 +0=3. Wait, maybe another way:\n\n6573 +75120:\n\n6573 +70000=76573\n\n76573 +5000=81573\n\n81573 +500=82073\n\n82073 +20=82093\n\nWait, that doesn't make sense. Wait, 75120 is 70000 +5000 +120. So 6573 +70000=76573; 76573 +5000=81573; 81573 +120=81693. Yes, that's correct.\n\nThen add 288300:\n\n81693 +288300. Let's