e intermediate steps. Let me check each multiplication again.\n\nFirst, 916 x 1 = 916. Correct.\n\n916 x 7: 900 x 7 = 6300, 16 x 7 = 112. 6300 + 112 = 6412. Shifted left by one, so 641,20. Wait, 6412 shifted left by one is 64120. Yes.\n\n916 x 9: 900 x 9 = 8100, 16 x 9 = 144. 8100 + 144 = 8244. Shifted left by two positions, so 824,400. Correct.\n\nNow adding:\n\nFirst, 916 (which is 00916) plus 64120 (which is 064120) plus 824400 (which is 0824400). Let's add them step by step.\n\nFirst, 00916 + 064120. Let's line them up:\n\n00916\n\n+064120\n\n= 065036. Then add 0824400:\n\n065036\n\n+0824400\n\n= 0889,436. So total is 889,436.\n\nWait, but let me check with another method to be sure. Maybe using the distributive property.\n\n916 x 971 can be written as 916 x (900 + 70 + 1). Let's compute that.\n\n916 x 900 = 916 x 9 x 100 = 8,244 x 100 = 824,400.\n\n916 x 70 = 916 x 7 x 10 = 6,412 x 10 = 64,120.\n\n916 x 1 = 916.\n\nNow add those three results: 824,400 + 64,120 + 916.\n\nFirst, 824,400 + 64,120. Let's compute:\n\n824,400 + 60,000 = 884,400\n\n884,400 + 4,120 = 888,520\n\nThen add 916: 888,520 + 916 = 889,436. Same result. Okay, so that seems correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the calculator method. But since I don't have a calculator, perhaps another check.\n\nLet me see, 916 x 971. Let's approximate to check if 889,436 is reasonable.\n\n916 is approximately 900, 900 x 971 = 900 x 900 + 900 x 71 = 810,000 + 63,900 = 873,900. Then 16 x 971 = 15,536. So total approx 873,900 + 15,536 = 889,436. That matches. So that seems correct.\n\nTherefore, the product of 916 and 971 is 889,436.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 916 and 971 is \\boxed{889436}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 916 and 971, we can use the standard multiplication method:\n\n1. Multiply 916 by the ones digit (1):\n   \\[\n   916 \\times 1 = 916\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 916 by the tens digit (7) and shift the result one position to the left:\n   \\[\n   916 \\times 7 = 6412 \\quad \\text{(shifted left by one position: 64120)}\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 916 by the hundreds digit (9) and shift the result two positions to the left:\n   \\[\n   916 \\times 9 = 8244 \\quad \\text{(shifted left by two positions: 824400)}\n   \\]\n\n4. Add the results of the three multiplications:\n   \\[\n   916 + 64120 + 824400\n   \\]\n\n5. Break down the addition step-by-step:\n   - First, add 916 and 64120:\n     \\[\n     916 + 64120 = 65036\n     \\]\n   - Then, add 65036 and 824400:\n     \\[\n     65036 + 824400 = 889436\n     \\]\n\nThus, the product of 916 and 971 is \\(\\boxed{889436}\\).",
