\n7*80: 560. Correct.\n\n7*8: 56. Correct.\n\nAdding them up:\n\n280,000 + 56,000 = 336,000. Then +5,600 = 341,600. Then +24,000 = 365,600. Then +4,800 = 370,400. Then +480 = 370,880. Then +2,800 = 373,680. Then +560 = 374,240. Then +56 = 374,296. Hmm, seems consistent.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use another method to cross-verify. Let's try the standard multiplication algorithm.\n\nMultiply 767 by 488:\n\nFirst, write 767\ntimes 488\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit:\n\n8 * 767: 8*7=56, carryover 5; 8*6=48 +5=53, carryover 5; 8*7=56 +5=61. So that's 6156.\n\nNext, 80 * 767: 0*767=0, carryover 0; 8*767=6,136. So 6,1360.\n\nThen, 400 * 767: 0*767=0, carryover 0; 4*767=3,068. So 3,06800.\n\nNow, add them up:\n\n6156\n61360\n306800\n--------\nAdding these:\n\nFirst, 6156 + 61360. Let's do 6156 + 61360. 6156 + 61360 = 67,516.\n\nThen, add 306,800. 67,516 + 306,800 = 374,316.\n\nWait, that's different from the previous result. Wait, so now I get 374,316? But earlier I got 374,296. There's a discrepancy here. Which one is correct?\n\nHmm, so maybe I made a mistake in one of the methods. Let me check the second method again.\n\nFirst, multiplying 767 by 8:\n\n8*7=56, carryover 5.\n\n8*6=48 +5=53, carryover 5.\n\n8*7=56 +5=61. So 6156. Correct.\n\nThen, 767*80. Since 80 is 8*10, so 767*8=6,136, then add a zero: 61,360. Correct.\n\nThen, 767*400. 400 is 4*100, so 767*4=3,068, then add two zeros: 306,800. Correct.\n\nNow, adding 6,156 + 61,360 + 306,800.\n\nFirst, 6,156 + 61,360. Let's compute 6,156 + 61,360. 6,156 + 60,000 = 66,156. Then +1,360 = 67,516. Then add 306,800. 67,516 + 306,800. Let's do 67,516 + 300,000 = 367,516. Then +6,800 = 374,316. So according to this, the total is 374,316.\n\nBut earlier, when I broke down the numbers into 700, 60, 7 and 400, 80, 8, and multiplied and added, I got 374,296. So there's a difference of 20. Hmm, so which one is correct?\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the first method. Let me check that again.\n\nOriginal breakdown:\n\n767 = 700 + 60 + 7\n\n488 = 400 + 80 + 8\n\nMultiplying each component:\n\n700*400 = 280,000\n\n700*80 = 56,000\n\n700*8 = 5,600\n\n60*400 = 24,000\n\n60*80 = 4,800\n\n60*8 = 480\n\n7*400 = 2,800\n\n7*80 = 560\n\n7*8 = 56\n\nAdding all these:\n\n280,000 + 56,000 = 336,000\n\n336,000 + 5,600 = 341,600\n\n341,600 + 24,000 = 365,600\n\n365,600 + 4,800 = 370,400\n\n370,400 + 480 = 370,880\n\n370,880 + 2,800 = 373,680\n\n373,680 + 560 = 374,240\n\n374,240 + 56 = 374,296\n\nBut according to the standard multiplication, it's 374,316. So there's a discrepancy of 20. That's a problem. Which one is correct?\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in one of the multiplications. Let me check each component again.\n\nFirst, 700*400: 700*400. 7*4=28, then add four zeros: 280,000. Correct.\n\n700*80: 700*8=5,600, then add two zeros: 56,000. Correct.\n\n700*8: 5,600. Correct.\n\n60*400: 60*4=24, add three zeros: 24,000. Correct.\n\n60*80: 60*8=480, add three zeros: 4,800. Correct.\n\n60*8: 480. Correct.\n\n7*400: 7*4=28, add three zeros: 2,800. Correct.\n\n7*80: 7*8=56, add three zeros: 560. Correct.\n\n7*8: 56. Correct.\n\nAdding them all step by step:\n\n280,000 + 56,000 = 336,000. Correct.\n\n336,000 + 5,600 = 341,600. Correct.\n\n341,600 + 24,000 = 365,600. Correct.\n\n365,600 + 4,800 = 370,400. Correct.\n\n370,400 + 480 = 370,880. Correct.\n\n370,880 + 2,800 = 373,680. Correct.\n\n373,680 + 560 = 374,240. Correct.\n\n374,240 + 56 = 374,296. Correct.\n\nBut according to the standard multiplication, it's 374,316. So where is the mistake?\n\nWait, maybe I messed up the standard multiplication steps. Let me check that again.\n\nMultiplying 767 by 488:\n\nFirst, write 767\n\ntimes 488\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n8 * 767: 8*7=56, carryover 5; 8*6=48 +5=53, carryover 5; 8*7=56 +5=61. So 6156.\n\nThen, 80 * 767: 0*767=0, carryover 0; 8*767=6,136. So 61360.\n\nThen, 400 * 767: 0*767=0, carryover 0; 4*767=3,068. So 306800.\n\nNow, adding 6156 + 61360 + 306800.\n\nFirst, 6156 + 61360. Let's compute 6156 + 61360:\n\n6156 + 61360 = 67,516.\n\nThen, 67,516 + 306,800 = 374,316.\n\nBut according to the breakdown method, it's 374,296. So there's a difference of 20. Hmm. That's a problem. Which one is correct?\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in one of the multiplications. Let me check 767*80 again.\n\n767*80. 767*8=6,136. Then 6,136*10=61,360. Correct.\n\n767*400. 767*4=3,068. Then 3,068*100=306,800. Correct.\n\n767*8. 7*8=56, carryover 0. 6*8=48 +0=48. 7*8=56 +0=56. So 5656. Wait, hold on! Wait, no. Wait, when multiplying 767 by 8, isn't that 700*8 + 60*8 +7*8?\n\nWait, 700*8=5,600; 60*8=480; 7*8=56. So 5,600 + 480=6,080 +56=6,136. So that's correct. So 767*8=6,136. Then 767*80=61,360. Correct.\n\nSimilarly, 767*400=306,800. Correct.\n\nSo adding 61,360 + 306,800 = 368,160. Then add 6,156. 368,160 +6,156= 374,316. So according to this, the total is 374,316.\n\nBut according to the breakdown method, it's 374,296. So where is the discrepancy?\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the breakdown method. Let me check that again.\n\nBreaking down 767 into 700 +60 +7 and 488 into 400 +80 +8.\n\nMultiplying each component:\n\n700*400=280,000\n\n700*80=56,000\n\n700*8=5,600\n\n60*400=24,000\n\n60*80=4,800\n\n60*8=480\n\n7*400=2,800\n\n7*80=560\n\n7*8=56\n\nAdding all these:\n\n280,000 +56,000=336,000\n\n336,000 +5,600=341,600\n\n341,600 +24,000=365,600\n\n365,600 +4,800=370,400\n\n370,400 +480=370,880\n\n370,880 +2,800=373,680\n\n373,680 +560=374,240\n\n374,240 +56=374,296\n\nBut according to the standard multiplication, it's 374,316. So there's a difference of 20. That's a problem. Which one is correct?\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in one of the multiplications. Let me check 700*80 again. 700*80=56,000. Correct. 700*8=5,600. Correct. 60*400=24,000. Correct. 60*80=4,800. Correct. 60*8=480. Correct. 7*400=2,800. Correct. 7*80=560. Correct. 7*8=56. Correct.\n\nSo all components are correct. Then why the discrepancy?\n\nWait, maybe the standard multiplication is wrong. Let me check 767*80 again.\n\n767*80. 767*8=6,136. 6,136*10=61,360. Correct.\n\n767*400. 767*4=3,068. 3,068*100=306,800. Correct.\n\nAdding 61,360 +306,800=368,160. Then adding 767*8=6,136. 368,160 +6,136=374,296. Wait, hold on! Wait, in the standard multiplication, I added 6156 (from 8*767) +61,360 (from 80*767) +306,800 (from 400*767). But 6156 +61,360 +306,800=6156+61,360=67,516 +306,800=374,316. But if I instead do 767*8 +767*80 +767*400, that's 6,136 +61,360 +306,800=374,296. Wait, but 767*8 is 6,136. Then 767*80 is 61,360. Then 767*400 is 306,800. So 6,136 +61,360=67,496 +306,800=374,296. But in the standard multiplication, I added 6,156 (from 8*767) +61,360 +306,800=374,316. Wait, but 8*767 is 6,136, not 6,156. Wait, that's the mistake!\n\nWait, in the standard multiplication, when I multiplied 8*767, I got 6,156. But that's incorrect. Wait, 8*700=5,600; 8*60=480; 8*7=56. So 5,600 +480=6,080 +56=6,136. So 8*767=6,136. But in my previous calculation, I wrote 6,156. That's a mistake! So that's the error. So in the standard multiplication, the first step was 8*767=6,136, but I incorrectly wrote 6,156. Then, adding 6,136 +61,360 +306,800=6,136+61,360=67,496 +306,800=374,296. Which matches the breakdown method. So that's the mistake. I must have miscalculated 8*767 as 6,156 instead of 6,136. So that's why there was a discrepancy. So the correct product is 374,296.\n\nTherefore, the answer is 374,296.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 767 and 488 is \\boxed{374296}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 767 and 488, we can use the distributive property by breaking down the numbers into their components:\n\n767 can be broken down into \\(700 + 60 + 7\\)\n488 can be broken down into \\(400 + 80 + 8\\)\n\nWe then multiply each component of 767 by each component of 488 and sum the results:\n\n1. \\(700 \\times 400 = 280,000\\)\n2. \\(700 \\times 80 = 56,000\\)\n3. \\(700 \\times 8 = 5,600\\)\n4. \\(60 \\times 400 = 24,000\\)\n5. \\(60 \\times 80 = 4,800\\)\n6. \\(60 \\times 8 = 480\\)\n7. \\(7 \\times 400 = 2,800\\)\n8. \\(7 \\times 80 = 560\\)\n9. \\(7 \\times 8 = 56\\)\n\nAdding all these results together:\n\n\\[\n280,000 + 56,000 + 5,600 + 24,000 + 4,800 + 480 + 2,800 + 560 + 56\n\\]\n\nStep-by-step addition:\n\n1. \\(280,000 + 56,000 = 336,000\\)\n2. \\(336,000 + 5,600 = 341,600\\)\n3. \\(341,600 + 24,000 = 365,600\\)\n4. \\(365,600 + 4,800 = 370,400\\)\n5. \\(370,400 + 480 = 370,880\\)\n6. \\(370,880 + 2,800 = 373,680\\)\n7. \\(373,680 + 560 = 374,240\\)\n8. \\(374,240 + 56 = 374,296\\)\n\nThus, the product of 767 and 488 is \\(\\boxed{374296}\\).",
