Adding 388,500 + 62,160 gives 450,660. \n\nTherefore, the correct product of 580 and 777 is 450,660. \n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 580 and 777 is \\boxed{450660}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 580 and 777, we can break down 580 into 500 + 80 and use the distributive property:\n\n\\[\n580 \\times 777 = (500 + 80) \\times 777 = 500 \\times 777 + 80 \\times 777\n\\]\n\nFirst, calculate \\(500 \\times 777\\):\n\n\\[\n500 \\times 777 = 5 \\times 100 \\times 777 = 5 \\times 777 \\times 100\n\\]\n\nCalculating \\(777 \\times 5\\):\n\n\\[\n777 \\times 5 = 3885\n\\]\n\nThen multiplying by 100:\n\n\\[\n3885 \\times 100 = 388500\n\\]\n\nNext, calculate \\(80 \\times 777\\):\n\n\\[\n80 \\times 777 = 8 \\times 10 \\times 777 = 8 \\times 777 \\times 10\n\\]\n\nCalculating \\(777 \\times 8\\):\n\n\\[\n777 \\times 8 = 6216\n\\]\n\nThen multiplying by 10:\n\n\\[\n6216 \\times 10 = 62160\n\\]\n\nNow, add the two results together:\n\n\\[\n388500 + 62160 = 450660\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 580 and 777 is \\(\\boxed{450660}\\).",
