y 241 by 7 (hundreds place): 241*700 = 168,700. Write down 168,700.\n\nNow, add them up:\n\n  168,700\n+   1,687\n---------\n170,387\n\nYes, that's the same result. So that's correct.\n\nTherefore, the product of 241 and 707 is 170,387.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 241 and 707 is \\boxed{170387}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 241 and 707, we can use the distributive property. We break down the numbers into smaller parts and multiply each part step by step.\n\nFirst, we express 241 as \\(200 + 40 + 1\\) and 707 as \\(700 + 0 + 7\\). Then, we distribute each term of 241 across each term of 707:\n\n1. Multiply 200 by each term in 707:\n   \\[\n   200 \\times 700 = 140,000\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   200 \\times 0 = 0\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   200 \\times 7 = 1,400\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 40 by each term in 707:\n   \\[\n   40 \\times 700 = 28,000\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   40 \\times 0 = 0\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   40 \\times 7 = 280\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 1 by each term in 707:\n   \\[\n   1 \\times 700 = 700\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   1 \\times 0 = 0\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   1 \\times 7 = 7\n   \\]\n\nNext, we add all the results together:\n\\[\n140,000 + 0 + 1,400 + 28,000 + 0 + 280 + 700 + 0 + 7\n\\]\n\nAdding these step by step:\n\\[\n140,000 + 1,400 = 141,400\n\\]\n\\[\n141,400 + 28,000 = 169,400\n\\]\n\\[\n169,400 + 700 = 170,100\n\\]\n\\[\n170,100 + 280 = 170,380\n\\]\n\\[\n170,380 + 7 = 170,387\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 241 and 707 is \\(\\boxed{170387}\\).",
