 = 1\nSo that gives 11628. Okay, that's correct.\n\nThen, adding 323,000 to 11628:\n\n323,000\n+  1,1628\n------------\nAlign them:\n\n323,000\n+  1,1628\n= 334,628\n\nYes, because 323,000 + 1,000 = 324,000; 324,000 + 1628 = 334,628. So the total is 334,628.\n\nWait, but let me verify this with another method to make sure. Maybe breaking down the numbers into factors that are easier to multiply.\n\n646 x 518. Let's see. 646 can be written as 600 + 40 + 6. And 518 is 500 + 10 + 8. So, using distributive property:\n\n(600 + 40 + 6) x (500 + 10 + 8) = 600*500 + 600*10 + 600*8 + 40*500 + 40*10 + 40*8 + 6*500 + 6*10 + 6*8.\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n600*500 = 300,000\n\n600*10 = 6,000\n\n600*8 = 4,800\n\n40*500 = 20,000\n\n40*10 = 400\n\n40*8 = 320\n\n6*500 = 3,000\n\n6*10 = 60\n\n6*8 = 48\n\nNow, add all these together:\n\n300,000 + 6,000 = 306,000\n\n306,000 + 4,800 = 310,800\n\n310,800 + 20,000 = 330,800\n\n330,800 + 400 = 331,200\n\n331,200 + 320 = 331,520\n\n331,520 + 3,000 = 334,520\n\n334,520 + 60 = 334,580\n\n334,580 + 48 = 334,628\n\nSo, same result as before. 334,628. That seems consistent. So that's probably the correct answer.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using another method like rounding numbers to make multiplication easier. Let's try that.\n\n646 x 518. Let's round 518 to 500 + 18. So, 646 x 500 = 323,000. Then 646 x 18. Let's compute 646 x 10 = 6,460; 646 x 8 = 5,168. So 6,460 + 5,168 = 11,628. Then add 323,000 + 11,628 = 334,628. Same answer again. So that's three different methods giving the same result. Seems solid.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using a calculator to verify. But since I don't have a calculator here, but given that all manual methods give the same answer, I can be confident.\n\nWait, just to check, maybe I can compute 646 x 518 using another decomposition. Let's see, 646 is 600 + 46, and 518 is 500 + 18. So:\n\n(600 + 46) x (500 + 18) = 600*500 + 600*18 + 46*500 + 46*18.\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n600*500 = 300,000\n\n600*18 = 10,800\n\n46*500 = 23,000\n\n46*18: Let's compute 40*18 = 720, 6*18=108, so 720 + 108 = 828.\n\nNow add all together:\n\n300,000 + 10,800 = 310,800\n\n310,800 + 23,000 = 333,800\n\n333,800 + 828 = 334,628. Again, same result. So, definitely, 334,628 is the correct product.\n\nTherefore, after multiple methods and checks, I can conclude that the product of 646 and 518 is 334,628.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 646 and 518 is \\boxed{334628}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 646 and 518, we can use the distributive property:\n\nFirst, decompose the numbers:\n- \\(646 = 600 + 40 + 6\\)\n- \\(518 = 500 + 10 + 8\\)\n\nNow, apply the distributive property:\n\\[\n(600 + 40 + 6) \\times (500 + 10 + 8) = 600 \\times 500 + 600 \\times 10 + 600 \\times 8 + 40 \\times 500 + 40 \\times 10 + 40 \\times 8 + 6 \\times 500 + 6 \\times 10 + 6 \\times 8\n\\]\n\nCalculate each term:\n- \\(600 \\times 500 = 300000\\)\n- \\(600 \\times 10 = 6000\\)\n- \\(600 \\times 8 = 4800\\)\n- \\(40 \\times 500 = 20000\\)\n- \\(40 \\times 10 = 400\\)\n- \\(40 \\times 8 = 320\\)\n- \\(6 \\times 500 = 3000\\)\n- \\(6 \\times 10 = 60\\)\n- \\(6 \\times 8 = 48\\)\n\nAdd all the terms together:\n\\[\n300000 + 6000 + 4800 + 20000 + 400 + 320 + 3000 + 60 + 48\n\\]\n\nGroup and sum step by step:\n- \\(300000 + 6000 = 306000\\)\n- \\(306000 + 4800 = 310800\\)\n- \\(310800 + 20000 = 330800\\)\n- \\(330800 + 400 = 331200\\)\n- \\(331200 + 320 = 331520\\)\n- \\(331520 + 3000 = 334520\\)\n- \\(334520 + 60 = 334580\\)\n- \\(334580 + 48 = 334628\\)\n\nThus, the product of 646 and 518 is \\(\\boxed{334628}\\).",
