and 187 is \\boxed{132396}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 708 and 187, we can use the distributive property:\n\n1. Decompose 187 into 200 - 13:\n   \\[\n   708 \\times 187 = 708 \\times (200 - 13) = 708 \\times 200 - 708 \\times 13\n   \\]\n\n2. Calculate each part separately:\n   - \\(708 \\times 200\\):\n     \\[\n     708 \\times 200 = 141,600\n     \\]\n   - \\(708 \\times 13\\):\n     \\[\n     708 \\times 10 = 7,080 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 708 \\times 3 = 2,124\n     \\]\n     Adding these results:\n     \\[\n     7,080 + 2,124 = 9,204\n     \\]\n\n3. Subtract the second result from the first:\n   \\[\n   141,600 - 9,204 = 132,396\n   \\]\n\n4. Verification using the standard multiplication method:\n   - Multiply 708 by each digit of 187 and sum the results:\n     \\[\n     708 \\times 7 = 4,956\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     708 \\times 8 \\times 10 = 56,640\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     708 \\times 1 \\times 100 = 70,800\n     \\]\n   - Adding these results:\n     \\[\n     4,956 + 56,640 + 70,800 = 132,396\n     \\]\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 708 and 187 is \\(\\boxed{132396}\\).",
