ly, gives the same result as the other methods. Therefore, the product of 146 and 377 is indeed 55,042.\n\nJust to be absolutely sure, let me verify using another approach. Let's use the formula (a + b)(c + d) = ac + ad + bc + bd, where a=100, b=46, c=300, d=77.\n\nSo:\n\n(100 + 46)(300 + 77) = 100\u00d7300 + 100\u00d777 + 46\u00d7300 + 46\u00d777\n\nCompute each term:\n\n100\u00d7300 = 30,000\n\n100\u00d777 = 7,700\n\n46\u00d7300 = 13,800\n\n46\u00d777: Let's compute 46\u00d770=3,220 and 46\u00d77=322. So 3,220 + 322 = 3,542.\n\nNow add all together:\n\n30,000 + 7,700 = 37,700\n\n37,700 + 13,800 = 51,500\n\n51,500 + 3,542 = 55,042. \n\nSame result. So this confirms it again. Therefore, the product is 55,042.\n\nI think that's thorough enough. All methods lead to the same answer, so I can be confident that 146 \u00d7 377 = 55,042.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 146 and 377 is \\boxed{55042}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 146 and 377, we can break down the multiplication into smaller parts and use the distributive property:\n\n1. **Break down 377 into 300 + 70 + 7:**\n   - \\( 146 \\times 300 = 43,800 \\)\n   - \\( 146 \\times 70 = 10,220 \\)\n   - \\( 146 \\times 7 = 1,022 \\)\n\n2. **Add the results of each part:**\n   - \\( 43,800 + 10,220 = 54,020 \\)\n   - \\( 54,020 + 1,022 = 55,042 \\)\n\n3. **Verification using standard multiplication method:**\n   - Multiply 146 by 7: \\( 146 \\times 7 = 1,022 \\)\n   - Multiply 146 by 70 (shifted one position left): \\( 146 \\times 70 = 10,220 \\)\n   - Multiply 146 by 300 (shifted two positions left): \\( 146 \\times 300 = 43,800 \\)\n   - Add the partial products: \\( 1,022 + 10,220 + 43,800 = 55,042 \\)\n\n4. **Verification using another method (expanding the product):**\n   - \\( (100 + 46)(300 + 77) = 100 \\times 300 + 100 \\times 77 + 46 \\times 300 + 46 \\times 77 \\)\n   - Calculate each term:\n     - \\( 100 \\times 300 = 30,000 \\)\n     - \\( 100 \\times 77 = 7,700 \\)\n     - \\( 46 \\times 300 = 13,8