e a calculator here, perhaps breaking down 739 into 700 + 39. Let's try that.\n\n739 = 700 + 39. So 700 \u00d7 289 + 39 \u00d7 289.\n\nFirst, 700 \u00d7 289. 700 \u00d7 200 = 140,000; 700 \u00d7 80 = 56,000; 700 \u00d7 9 = 6,300. So 140,000 + 56,000 = 196,000; 196,000 + 6,300 = 202,300.\n\nThen, 39 \u00d7 289. Let's compute that. 39 is 40 - 1. So 40 \u00d7 289 = 11,560. Then subtract 1 \u00d7 289 = 289. So 11,560 - 289 = 11,271.\n\nNow, add 202,300 + 11,271. \n\n202,300 + 10,000 = 212,300  \n212,300 + 1,271 = 213,571. \n\nSame result again. Okay, so that's three different methods giving me 213,571. That seems pretty solid. \n\nAlternatively, maybe I can check using another multiplication approach. Let's see. \n\nIf I consider 739 \u00d7 289, perhaps I can rearrange the multiplication to make it easier. For example, 739 \u00d7 289 = 739 \u00d7 (300 - 11) = 739 \u00d7 300 - 739 \u00d7 11. Let's try that.\n\n739 \u00d7 300 = 221,700.  \n739 \u00d7 11 = 739 \u00d7 10 + 739 \u00d7 1 = 7,390 + 739 = 8,129.  \nSo 221,700 - 8,129 = 213,571. \n\nAgain, same answer. Wow, that's consistent. So all these different methods are leading me to 213,571. \n\nJust to make sure, maybe I can check with another perspective. Let's use the fact that 739 \u00d7 289 = (700 + 39)(200 + 80 + 9). Wait, that's similar to the first method. But we already did that. \n\nAlternatively, maybe use the standard multiplication algorithm step by step. Let's write it out:\n\n      739  \n    \u00d7 289  \n    --------  \n      739 \u00d7 9 = 6,651  \n      739 \u00d7 80 = 59,120  \n     739 \u00d7 200 = 147,800  \n    --------  \n  6,651  59,120 147,800  \n    66,771 65,771 213,571  \n    -----------------------  \n  213,571  \n\nWait, when adding 6,651 + 59,120 + 147,800, we can do it in parts. Let's add 6,651 + 59,120 first. \n\n6,651 + 59,120:  \n6,000 + 50,000 = 56,000  \n600 + 9,000 = 9,600  \n50 + 120 = 170  \n1 + 0 = 1  \nWait, that's not the right way. Let me do it properly:\n\n6,651  \n+59,120  \nStart from the right:  \n1 + 0 = 1  \n5 + 2 = 7  \n6 + 1 = 7  \n0 + 9 = 9  \n6 + 5 = 11  \nSo that's 65,771. Then add 147,800:\n\n65,771 + 147,800.  \n65,771 + 100,000 = 165,771  \n165,771 + 40,000 = 205,771  \n205,771 + 7,000 = 212,771  \n212,771 + 800 = 213,571  \n213,571 + 0 = 213,571. \n\nSame result. Okay, so all methods converge to 213,571. \n\nJust to be thorough, maybe I can check with another example. Let's take a simpler multiplication and see if my multiplication method works. For example, 12 \u00d7 13. \n\nUsing the standard method:  \n12 \u00d7 3 = 36  \n12 \u00d7 10 = 120  \n12 \u00d7 0 = 0  \nAdding them: 36 + 120 = 156. Which is correct. \n\nAlternatively, breaking down 13 into 10 + 3. 12 \u00d7 10 = 120, 12 \u00d7 3 = 36. 120 + 36 = 156. Correct. \n\nSo my multiplication method works for smaller numbers, which gives me more confidence that it's correct for the larger numbers. \n\nTherefore, after multiple methods and checks, I can be confident that the product of 739 and 289 is 213,571.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 739 and 289 is \\boxed{213571}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 739 and 289, we can break down the multiplication into smaller parts and use the distributive property. Here are the key steps:\n\n1. **Break down 289 into 9, 80, and 200:**\n   - \\( 739 \\times 9 \\)\n   - \\( 739 \\times 80 \\)\n   - \\( 739 \\times 200 \\)\n\n2. **Calculate each part separately:**\n   - \\( 739 \\times 9 = 6651 \\)\n   - \\( 739 \\times 80 = 59120 \\)\n   - \\( 739 \\times 200 = 147800 \\)\n\n3. **Sum the results:**\n   - Add \\( 6651 \\) and \\( 59120 \\):\n     \\[\n     6651 + 59120 = 65771\n     \\]\n   - Add the result to \\( 147800 \\):\n     \\[\n     65771 + 147800 = 213571\n     \\]\n\n4. **Verification using different methods:**\n   - Breaking down 739 into 700 + 39 and multiplying:\n     \\[\n     (700 + 39) \\times 289 = 700 \\times 289 + 39 \\times 289 = 202300 + 11271 = 213571\n     \\]\n   - Rearranging the multiplication:\n     \\[\n     739 \\times (300 - 11) = 739 \\times 300 - 739 \\times 11 = 221700 - 8129 = 213571\n     \\]\n\nAll methods confirm that the product of 739 and 289 is \\(\\boxed{213571}\\).",
