check the addition again. 610,400 + 21,364. Breaking it down: 610,400 + 20,000 = 630,400. Then 630,400 + 1,000 = 631,400. Then 631,400 + 364 = 631,764. Yeah, that seems correct.\n\nSo, the total product is 631,764. Let me verify this with another method to make sure I didn't make a mistake.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the calculator method. Let me compute 763 \u00d7 828. Let's see. 763 \u00d7 800 = 610,400. 763 \u00d7 20 = 15,260. 763 \u00d7 8 = 6,104. Then adding those together: 610,400 + 15,260 = 625,660; 625,660 + 6,104 = 631,764. Yep, same result. So that seems to check out.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use another approach. Let's think of 828 as 800 + 28. So, 763 \u00d7 828 = 763 \u00d7 (800 + 28) = 763\u00d7800 + 763\u00d728. We already know 763\u00d7800 is 610,400. Now, 763\u00d728. Let's compute that. 763\u00d720 = 15,260 and 763\u00d78 = 6,104. So, 15,260 + 6,104 = 21,364. Then, 610,400 + 21,364 = 631,764. Same answer again. So, that's consistent.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the standard algorithm again but check each step. Let's redo the multiplication:\n\nMultiplying 763 by 828:\n\nFirst, multiply 763 by 8: 700\u00d78=5600, 60\u00d78=480, 3\u00d78=24. Sum: 5600+480=6080+24=6104. Correct.\n\nNext, multiply 763 by 2 (tens place): 763\u00d72=1526. Since it's the tens place, add a zero: 15260. Correct.\n\nNext, multiply 763 by 8 (hundreds place): 763\u00d78=6104. Add two zeros: 610400. Correct.\n\nAdding 6104 + 15260 + 610400. Let's do this step by step:\n\n6104 + 15260: 6104 + 15260. Let's add 6000 + 15000 = 21000. Then 104 + 260 = 364. So total 21364. Then 21364 + 610400. 21364 + 610400. 20000 + 610400 = 630400. Then 1364 + 0 = 1364. So 630400 + 1364 = 631,764. Correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the vertical multiplication method step by step:\n\n      763\n    \u00d7 828\n    --------\n      6104  (763 \u00d7 8)\n     15260   (763 \u00d7 20, shifted one position to the left)\n    610400   (763 \u00d7 800, shifted two positions to the left)\n    --------\n    631764   (sum all three)\n\nYes, that's the same as before. So, all methods lead to 631,764. Therefore, I can be confident that the product of 763 and 828 is 631,764.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 763 and 828 is \\boxed{631764}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 763 and 828, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. Multiply 763 by the units digit (8) of 828:\n   \\[\n   763 \\times 8 = 6104\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 763 by the tens digit (2) of 828, then add a zero:\n   \\[\n   763 \\times 2 = 1526 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 1526 \\times 10 = 15260\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 763 by the hundreds digit (8) of 828, then add two zeros:\n   \\[\n   763 \\times 8 = 6104 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 6104 \\times 100 = 610400\n   \\]\n\n4. Add all the partial products together:\n   \\[\n   6104 + 15260 + 610400 = 631764\n   \\]\n\nThus, the product of 763 and 828 is \\(\\boxed{631764}\\).",
