om the right:\n\n9 (units place) * 607 = 5463.\n\n7 (tens place) * 607 = 42,490.\n\n8 (hundreds place) * 607 = 485,600.\n\nNow add them up:\n\n5463\n\n+42,490\n\n+485,600\n\nFirst, 5463 + 42,490:\n\n5,463 + 42,490. Let's add 5,000 + 42,000 = 47,000. Then 463 + 490 = 953. So total is 47,000 + 953 = 47,953.\n\nThen 47,953 + 485,600:\n\n47,953 + 400,000 = 447,953\n\n447,953 + 85,600 = 533,553.\n\nYes, same result. So that's correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use another approach. Let's use the fact that 879 is 800 + 70 + 9, as before, but maybe compute 607*879 as 607*(800 + 70 + 9) = 607*800 + 607*70 + 607*9. Which is 485,600 + 42,490 + 5,463. Let's add those:\n\n485,600 + 42,490 = 528,090. Then 528,090 + 5,463 = 533,553. Same answer. So all methods lead to 533,553. Therefore, I can be confident that the product is 533,553.\n\nBut just to make sure, let me try multiplying 607 by 879 using another decomposition. For example, 607 can be 600 + 7, and 879 as 800 + 70 + 9. So:\n\n(600 + 7)(800 + 70 + 9) = 600*800 + 600*70 + 600*9 + 7*800 + 7*70 + 7*9. Which is 480,000 + 42,000 + 5,400 + 5,600 + 490 + 63. Let's add these:\n\n480,000 + 42,000 = 522,000\n\n522,000 + 5,400 = 527,400\n\n527,400 + 5,600 = 533,000\n\n533,000 + 490 = 533,490\n\n533,490 + 63 = 533,553. Yep, same result. So all methods confirm that the product is 533,553.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the vertical multiplication method step by step.\n\nMultiplying 607 by 879:\n\nFirst, write 607 x 9:\n\n7 x 9 = 63, write down 3, carry over 6.\n\n0 x 9 = 0 +6 =6.\n\n6 x9=54 +0=54. So 5463.\n\nNext, multiply 607 by 70 (tens place):\n\nBut 70 is 7*10, so shift one position to the left and multiply 607 by 7:\n\n7 x7=49, write down 9, carry over 4.\n\n0 x7=0 +4=4.\n\n6 x7=42 +0=42. So 4249. Then add two zeros: 42,490.\n\nNext, multiply 607 by 800 (hundreds place):\n\n800 is 8*100. Multiply 607 by 8:\n\n8x7=56, write down 6, carry over 5.\n\n0x8=0 +5=5.\n\n6x8=48 +0=48. So 4856. Then add three zeros: 485,600.\n\nNow add the three partial products:\n\n5463\n\n42,490\n\n485,600\n\nAdding 5463 + 42,490:\n\n5,463 + 42,490. Let's do 5,000 + 42,000 = 47,000. Then 463 + 490 = 953. So total 47,000 + 953 = 47,953.\n\nThen add 485,600:\n\n47,953 + 485,600. 47,953 + 400,000 = 447,953. Then 447,953 + 85,600 = 533,553. Same result.\n\nTherefore, regardless of the method used, the product of 607 and 879 is 533,553. I think that's solid. I don't see any mistakes in my calculations, and multiple methods cross-check the result. So I'm confident that's the correct answer.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 607 and 879 is \\boxed{533553}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 607 and 879, we can use the distributive property:\n\nFirst, decompose 607 into \\(600 + 7\\) and 879 into \\(800 + 70 + 9\\). Then, apply the distributive property:\n\n\\[\n(600 + 7) \\times (800 + 70 + 9) = 600 \\times 800 + 600 \\times 70 + 600 \\times 9 + 7 \\times 800 + 7 \\times 70 + 7 \\times 9\n\\]\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n\\[\n600 \\times 800 = 480000\n\\]\n\\[\n600 \\times 70 = 42000\n\\]\n\\[\n600 \\times 9 = 5400\n\\]\n\\[\n7 \\times 800 = 5600\n\\]\n\\[\n7 \\times 70 = 490\n\\]\n\\[\n7 \\times 9 = 63\n\\]\n\nAdding all these results together:\n\n\\[\n480000 + 42000 + 5400 + 5600 + 490 + 63\n\\]\n\nBreaking down the addition step-by-step:\n\n\\[\n480000 + 42000 = 522000\n\\]\n\\[\n522000 + 5400 = 527400\n\\]\n\\[\n527400 + 5600 = 533000\n\\]\n\\[\n533000 + 490 = 533490\n\\]\n\\[\n533490 + 63 = 533553\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 607 and 879 is \\(\\boxed{533553}\\).",
