So 115,200 - 1,280 = 113,920. \n\nYes, that works too. So that's another way to get the same answer. So, 113,920. \n\nTherefore, after multiple methods and checking, I can confirm that the product of 356 and 320 is 113,920. \n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 356 and 320 is \\boxed{113920}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 356 and 320, we can use the distributive property:\n\nFirst, break down the numbers:\n- \\(356 = 300 + 50 + 6\\)\n- \\(320 = 300 + 20\\)\n\nNow, distribute each term in the first number across the second number:\n\\[\n(300 + 50 + 6) \\times (300 + 20)\n\\]\n\nCalculate each term separately:\n\\[\n300 \\times 300 = 90,000\n\\]\n\\[\n300 \\times 20 = 6,000\n\\]\n\\[\n50 \\times 300 = 15,000\n\\]\n\\[\n50 \\times 20 = 1,000\n\\]\n\\[\n6 \\times 300 = 1,800\n\\]\n\\[\n6 \\times 20 = 120\n\\]\n\nAdd all these results together:\n\\[\n90,000 + 6,000 + 15,000 + 1,000 + 1,800 + 120\n\\]\n\nCombine the sums step by step:\n\\[\n90,000 + 6,000 = 96,000\n\\]\n\\[\n96,000 + 15,000 = 111,000\n\\]\n\\[\n111,000 + 1,000 = 112,000\n\\]\n\\[\n112,000 + 1,800 = 113,800\n\\]\n\\[\n113,800 + 120 = 113,920\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 356 and 320 is \\(\\boxed{113920}\\).",
